ep length alpha from the current point\n( theta_k , phi_k ), is acceptable (see filter_line_search for the\nrules). gtp is the predicted change in the objective along the full\nstep ( for the line search; the trust region passes the\nquadratic model's , with alpha=1 ). f_type is set if the\nswitching condition held (so the step was judged on the objective alone,\nand must not enlarge the filter). The trial point must also be\nacceptable to the filter itself: , and not\ndominated by any filter entry ( or for every entry j ). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( sqpopt_filter_type ), intent(in) :: me real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: theta_k violation and objective at the current point real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: phi_k violation and objective at the current point real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: gtp predicted change in the objective along the full step real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: alpha step length real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: theta_t violation and objective at the trial point real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: phi_t violation and objective at the trial point logical, intent(out) :: f_type true if the switching condition held Return Value logical procedure, public :: record => filter_augment private  subroutine filter_augment (me, theta_k, phi_k) augment the filter with the current point ( theta_k , phi_k ), with\nmargins: the entry is added, and any existing entries\nit dominates are removed. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( sqpopt_filter_type ), intent(inout) :: me real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: theta_k violation and objective at the current point real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: phi_k violation and objective at the current point procedure, public :: min_step => filter_min_step private pure function filter_min_step (me, theta_k, gtp) result(alpha_min) Wächter & Biegler's minimum step length : below it,\nno trial step can be acceptable (so the line search should give up and\ngo to feasibility restoration). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes N