t measure of the violation, so it can\noccasionally end slightly outside). Shared by funnel_line_search and\nthe trust region's funnel acceptance. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( sqpopt_funnel_type ), intent(inout) :: me real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: theta_k constraint violation at the current point procedure, public :: accept => funnel_step_acceptable private  function funnel_step_acceptable (me, theta_k, phi_k, pred, theta_t, phi_t, f_type) result(ok) whether a trial point with violation theta_t and objective phi_t is\nacceptable to the funnel, from the current point ( theta_k , phi_k )\n(see funnel_line_search for the rules). pred is the predicted\ndecrease in the objective ( for the line search; the\ntrust region passes the quadratic model's decrease q ). f_type is set\nif the switching condition held (so the step was judged on the objective\nalone, and must not shrink the funnel). Doesn't change the funnel: the\ncaller shrinks it after accepting an h-type step (see funnel_shrink ). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( sqpopt_funnel_type ), intent(in) :: me real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: theta_k violation and objective at the current point real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: phi_k violation and objective at the current point real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: pred predicted decrease in the objective real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: theta_t violation and objective at the trial point real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: phi_t violation and objective at the trial point logical, intent(out) :: f_type true if the switching condition held Return Value logical procedure, public :: record => funnel_shrink private  subroutine funnel_shrink (me, theta_k, theta_t) shrink the funnel after an accepted h-type step from violation theta_k to theta_t (see update for the two rules). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( sqpopt_funnel_type ), intent(inout) :: me real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: theta_k violation at the current point real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: theta_t violation at the accepted point procedure, public :: restoration => funnel_shrink_restoration private  subroutine funnel_shrink_restoration (me, theta_k) shrink the funnel toward the current violation theta_k before a\nfeasibility restoration step, so the iterations can't cycle back to the\ncurrent point: . Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( sqpopt_funnel_type ), intent(inout) :: me real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: theta_k violation at the current point procedure, public :: acceptable => funnel_point_acceptable private  function funnel_point_acceptable (me, theta) result(ok) whether a point with violation theta is inside the funnel, (always true before the funnel is initialized). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( sqpopt_funnel_type ), intent(in) :: me real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: theta constraint violation Return Value logical Source Code type , public :: sqpopt_funnel_type !! options and state of the funnel (the `funnel` component of !! [[sqpopt_linesearch_type]]), with the default values of the Uno !! solver. real ( wp ) :: width_min = 1.0_wp !! initial funnel width  \\tau_0 = \\max(  this, `width_fact` !!  \\times\\,\\theta_0)  real ( wp ) :: width_fact = 1.5_wp !! see `width_min` real ( wp ) :: beta = 0.9999_wp !! an h-type step must reach  \\theta \\le \\beta\\tau  ( 0<\\beta<1 ) real ( wp ) :: kappa = 0.5_wp !! after an h-type step, the new width is (at least) the convex !! combination  \\kappa\\theta_k + (1-\\kappa)\\theta_t  (see `update`) integer :: update = 1 !! funnel width update after an h-type step: `1` = !!  \\max(\\beta\\tau, \\kappa\\theta_k+(1-\\kappa)\\theta_t)  if the !! violation decreased, else  \\beta\\tau ; `2` =  \\kappa\\tau + !! (1-\\kappa)\\theta_t  real ( wp ) :: delta = 0.999_wp !! switching condition constant  \\delta : an f-type step needs !!  \\alpha(-g&#94;Tp) > \\delta\\theta_k&#94;{s_\\theta}  real ( wp ) :: s_theta = 2.0_wp !! switching condition exponent  s_\\theta  real ( wp ) :: eta = 1.0e-4_wp !! Armijo constant  \\eta  for f-type steps logical :: require_current = . false . !! also require every trial point to be acceptable with respect to !! the current point:  \\theta_t < \\beta\\theta_k  or !!  \\varphi_t \\le \\varphi_k - \\gamma\\theta_t  real ( wp ) :: gamma = 1.0e-3_wp !!  \\gamma  in `require_current` ! internal state (not user options -- persists across major iterations): logical :: ready = . false . !! whether the funnel width below has been initialized real ( wp ) :: width = 0.0_wp !! the funnel width  \\tau  contains procedure , public :: prepare => funnel_prepare_state procedure , public :: accept => funnel_step_acceptable procedure , public :: record => funnel_shrink procedure , public :: restoration => funnel_shrink_restoration procedure , public :: acceptable => funnel_point_acceptable end type sqpopt_funnel_type","tags":"","url":"type/sqpopt_funnel_type.html"},{"title":"sqpopt_qp_solver_type – sqpopt ","text":"type, public :: sqpopt_qp_solver_type workspace and options for the QP subproblem solver. Inherits type~~sqpopt_qp_solver_type~~InheritsGraph type~sqpopt_qp_solver_type sqpopt_qp_solver_type type~sqpopt_dense_qp_type sqpopt_dense_qp_type type~sqpopt_qp_solver_type->type~sqpopt_dense_qp_type dense_qp type~sqpopt_reduced_hessian_qp_type sqpopt_reduced_hessian_qp_type type~sqpopt_qp_solver_type->type~sqpopt_reduced_hessian_qp_type sparse_qp Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Type Type This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a derived type to the parent type which it\nextends. Dashed arrows point from a derived type to the other\ntypes it contains as a components, with a label listing the name(s) of\nsaid component(s). Inherited by type~~sqpopt_qp_solver_type~~InheritedByGraph type~sqpopt_qp_solver_type sqpopt_qp_solver_type type~sqpopt_restoration_type sqpopt_restoration_type type~sqpopt_restoration_type->type~sqpopt_qp_solver_type qp type~sqpopt_type sqpop