lp Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Called by proc~~inertia_correct~~CalledByGraph proc~inertia_correct sqpopt_inertia_type%inertia_correct proc~direct_qp_step direct_qp_step proc~direct_qp_step->proc~inertia_correct proc~sqpopt_iterate sqpopt_iterate proc~sqpopt_iterate->proc~inertia_correct proc~solve_qp_subproblem sqpopt_qp_solver_type%solve_qp_subproblem proc~sqpopt_iterate->proc~solve_qp_subproblem proc~restoration_phase_step sqpopt_restoration_type%restoration_phase_step proc~sqpopt_iterate->proc~restoration_phase_step proc~trust_region_step sqpopt_trust_region_type%trust_region_step proc~sqpopt_iterate->proc~trust_region_step proc~solve_qp_subproblem->proc~direct_qp_step proc~sqpopt_solve sqpopt_type%sqpopt_solve proc~sqpopt_solve->proc~sqpopt_iterate proc~nlls_solve sqpopt_nlls_type%nlls_solve proc~nlls_solve->proc~sqpopt_solve proc~restoration_phase_step->proc~solve_qp_subproblem proc~trust_region_step->proc~solve_qp_subproblem Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine inertia_correct ( me , kkt , hessian , jac , status , changed , ok , n_negative ) class ( sqpopt_inertia_type ), intent ( inout ) :: me type ( sqpopt_kkt_type ), intent ( inout ) :: kkt !! the KKT matrix (see [[sqpopt_kkt_module]]) type ( sqpopt_hessian_type ), intent ( inout ) :: hessian !! the Hessian (its `shift` is updated) type ( sqpopt_sparse_matrix ), intent ( in ) :: jac !! the constraint Jacobian `dimension(m,n)` integer , dimension (:), intent ( in ) :: status !! the working set: nonzero for each general row, then each !! variable bound, that is in it `dimension(m+n)` logical , intent ( out ) :: changed !! whether the shift was increased logical , intent ( out ) :: ok !! whether no negative curvature is left (see above) integer , optional , intent ( out ) :: n_negative !! the number of directions of negative curvature !! found with the shift on entry (`-1` if nothing !! was factored) real ( wp ) :: shift_max logical :: first , factored changed = . false . ok = . false . if ( present ( n_negative )) n_negative = - 1 if (. not . me % enabled ) return shift_max = hessian % shift_max * hessian % magnitude () first = . true . do call kkt % factor ( hessian , jac , status , factored ) if (. not . factored ) then ! (fall back on the matrix-free tests from here on) me % enabled = . false . return end if if ( first . and . present ( n_negative )) n_negative = kkt % n_negative if ( kkt % n_negative == 0 ) then ok = . true . exit end if if ( hessian % shift >= shift_max ) exit call me % raise ( hessian ) changed = . true . first = . false . end do if ( ok . and . changed ) me % shift_last = hessian % shift end subroutine inertia_correct","tags":"","url":"proc/inertia_correct.html"},{"title":"inertia_raise – sqpopt","text":"private  subroutine inertia_raise(me, hessian) increase the Hessian's shift to the next one to try (see the module\ndocumentation): 8 times the current one, and at least shift_min times\nthe size of the Hessian, or a third of the last shift that was needed;\nat most shift_max times the size of the Hessian. Type Bound sqpopt_inertia_type Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( sqpopt_inertia_type ), intent(in) :: me type( sqpopt_hessian_type ), intent(inout) :: hessian the Hessian (its shift is updated) Calls proc~~inertia_raise~~CallsGraph proc~inertia_raise sqpopt_inertia_type%inertia_raise proc~hessian_size sqpopt_hessian_type%hessian_size proc~inertia_raise->proc~hessian_size Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Called by proc~~inertia_raise~~CalledByGraph proc~inertia_raise sqpopt_inertia_type%inertia_raise proc~inertia_correct sqpopt_inertia_type%inertia_correct proc~inertia_correct->proc~inertia_raise proc~sqpopt_iterate sqpopt_iterate proc~sqpopt_iterate->proc~inertia_raise proc~sqpopt_iterate->proc~inertia_correct proc~solve_qp_subproblem sqpopt_qp_solver_type%solve_qp_subproblem proc~sqpopt_iterate->proc~solve_qp_subproblem proc~restoration_phase_step sqpopt_restoration_type%restoration_phase_step proc~sqpopt_iterate->proc~restoration_phase_step proc~trust_region_step sqpopt_trust_region_type%trust_region_step proc~sqpopt_iterate->proc~trust_region_step proc~direct_qp_step direct_qp_step proc~direct_qp_step->proc~inertia_correct proc~sqpopt_solve sqpopt_type%sqpopt_solve proc~sqpopt_solve->proc~sqpopt_iterate proc~nlls_solve sqpopt_nlls_type%nlls_solve proc~nlls_solve->proc~sqpopt_solve proc~solve_qp_subproblem->proc~direct_qp_step proc~restoration_phase_step->proc~solve_qp_subproblem proc~trust_region_step->proc~solve_qp_subproblem Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine inertia_raise ( me , hessian ) class ( sqpopt_inertia_type ), intent ( in ) :: me type ( sqpopt_hessian_type ), intent ( inout ) :: hessian !! the Hessian (its `shift` is updated) real ( wp ) :: shift shift = hessian % shift_min * hessian % magnitude () if ( me % shift_last > 0.0_wp ) shift = max ( shift , me % shift_last / 3.0_wp ) shift = max ( shift , 8.0_wp * hessian % shift ) hessian % shift = min ( shift , hessian % shift_max * hessian % magnitude ()) end subroutine inertia_raise","tags":"","url":"proc/inertia_raise.html"},{"title":"dense_start – sqpopt","text":"private  subroutine dense_start(me, n, irow, icol, ok, threads, signs) keep the pattern, and allocate the dense matrices. ok is false if the\norder exceeds dense_max_order , or the matrices can't be allocated. threads and signs are not used (this backend pivots, and is\nsingle-threaded). Type Bound sqpopt_dense_ldl_type Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( sqpopt_dense_ldl_type ), intent(inout) :: me integer, intent(in) :: n order of the matrix integer, intent(in), dimension(:) :: irow row indices of the entries dimension(nnz) integer, intent(in), dimension(:) :: icol column indices of the entries dimension(nnz) logical, intent(out) :: ok whether the backend is ready integer, intent(in), optional :: threads (not used) integer, intent(in), optional, dimension(:) :: signs (not used) Source Code subroutine dense_start ( me , n , irow , icol , ok , threads , signs ) class ( sqpopt_dense_ldl_type ), intent ( inout ) :: me integer , intent ( in ) :: n !! order of the matrix integer , dimension (:), intent ( in ) :: irow !! row indices of the entries `dimension(nnz)` integer , dimension (:), intent ( in ) :: icol !! column indices of the entries `dimension(nnz)` logical , intent ( out ) :: ok !! whether the backend is ready integer , optional , intent ( in ) :: threads !! (not used) integer , dimension (:), optional , intent ( in ) :: signs !! (not used) integer :: alloc_stat ok = . false . if ( present ( threads ) . or . present ( signs )) continue ! (not used) if ( n > dense_max_order ) return allocate ( me % a ( n , n ), stat = alloc_stat ) if ( alloc_stat == 0 ) allocate ( me % lu ( n , n ), stat = alloc_stat ) if ( alloc_stat == 0 ) allocate ( me % piv ( n ), stat = alloc_stat ) if ( alloc_stat /= 0 ) then me % out_of_memory = . true . call me % free () return end if me % irow = irow me % icol = icol me % n = n ok = . true . end subroutine dense_start","tags":"","url":"proc/dense_start.html"},{"title":"dense_refactor – sqpopt","text":"private  subroutine dense_refactor(me, val, ok) form the dense matrix from the values val , count its inertia, and\nfactor it (see the module documentation). Type Bound sqpopt_dense_ldl_type Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( sqpopt_dense_ldl_type ), intent(inout) :: me real(kind=wp), intent(in), dimension(:) :: val values of the entries dimension(nnz) logical, intent(out) :: ok whether the factorization succeeded Calls proc~~dense_refactor~~CallsGraph proc~dense_refactor sqpopt_dense_ldl_type%dense_refactor proc~dense_symmetric_inertia dense_symmetric_inertia proc~dense_refactor->proc~dense_symmetric_inertia proc~lu_factor_null_safe lu_factor_null_safe proc~dense_refactor->proc~lu_factor_null_safe proc~sqpopt_all_finite sqpopt_all_finite proc~dense_refactor->proc~sqpopt_all_finite Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine dense_refactor ( me , val , ok ) class ( sqpopt_dense_ldl_type ), intent ( inout ) :: me real ( wp ), dimension (:), intent ( in ) :: val !! values of the entries `dimension(nnz)` logical , intent ( out ) :: ok !! whether the factorization succeeded integer :: k , i , j , n_positive ok = . false . me % inertia_known = . true . if (. not . sqpopt_all_finite ( val )) return do j = 1 , me % n do i = 1 , me % n me % a ( i , j ) = 0.0_wp end do end do do k = 1 , size ( val ) i = me % irow ( k ) j = me % icol ( k ) me % a ( i , j ) = me % a ( i , j ) + val ( k ) if ( i /= j ) me % a ( j , i ) = me % a ( j , i ) + val ( k ) end do call dense_symmetric_inertia ( me % a , n_positive , me % n_negative , me % n_null , zero_tol = dense_zero_tol ) do j = 1 , me % n do i = 1 , me % n me % lu ( i , j ) = me % a ( i , j ) end do end do call lu_factor_null_safe ( me % lu , me % piv ) ok = . true . end subroutine dense_refactor","tags":"","url":"proc/dense_refactor.html"},{"title":"lu_factor_null_safe – sqpopt","text":"private pure subroutine lu_factor_null_safe(a, piv) in-place LU factorization with partial pivoting of the dense matrix a , in which a negligible pivot (a null column, below the diagonal) is\nreplaced by a large one, so that the factorization never fails (see the\nmodule documentation). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(inout), dimension(:,:) :: a matrix, overwritten by its L (unit, below the diagonal)\nand U factors integer, intent(out), dimension(:) :: piv piv(p) is the row swapped with row p at step p Called by proc~~lu_factor_null_safe~~CalledByGraph proc~lu_factor_null_safe lu_factor_null_safe proc~dense_refactor sqpopt_dense_ldl_type%dense_refactor proc~dense_refactor->proc~lu_factor_null_safe Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code pure subroutine lu_factor_null_safe ( a , piv ) real ( wp ), dimension (:,:), intent ( inout ) :: a !! matrix, overwritten by its `L` (unit, below the diagonal) !! and `U` factors integer , dimension (:), intent ( out ) :: piv !! `piv(p)` is the row swapped with row `p` at step `p` integer :: i , j , p , n real ( wp ) :: amax , tol , big , t n = size ( a , 1 ) amax = 0.0_wp do j = 1 , n do i = 1 , n amax = max ( amax , abs ( a ( i , j ))) end do end do tol = 1.0e-14_wp * max ( amax , tiny ( 1.0_wp )) big = max ( amax , 1.0_wp ) / sqrt ( epsilon ( 1.0_wp )) do p = 1 , n ! the pivot: the largest element of column p, on or below the diagonal piv ( p ) = p do i = p + 1 , n if ( abs ( a ( i , p )) > abs ( a ( piv ( p ), p ))) piv ( p ) = i end do if ( piv ( p ) /= p ) then do j = 1 , n t = a ( p , j ) a ( p , j ) = a ( piv ( p ), j ) a ( piv ( p ), j ) = t end do end if if ( abs ( a ( p , p )) <= tol ) then a ( p , p ) = big ! (a null column: its component of a solution becomes negligible) end if do i = p + 1 , n a ( i , p ) = a ( i , p ) / a ( p , p ) do j = p + 1 , n a ( i , j ) = a ( i , j ) - a ( i , p ) * a ( p , j ) end do end do end do end subroutine lu_factor_null_safe","tags":"","url":"proc/lu_factor_null_safe.html"},{"title":"dense_back_solve – sqpopt","text":"private  subroutine dense_back_solve(me, v, ok) one solve with the LU factors, without refinement. Type Bound sqpopt_dense_ldl_type Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( sqpopt_dense_ldl_type ), intent(inout) :: me real(kind=wp), intent(inout), dimension(:) :: v the right-hand side, overwritten by the solution logical, intent(out) :: ok whether it was solved Calls proc~~dense_back_solve~~CallsGraph proc~dense_back_solve sqpopt_dense_ldl_type%dense_back_solve proc~sqpopt_all_finite sqpopt_all_finite proc~dense_back_solve->proc~sqpopt_all_finite Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine dense_back_solve ( me , v , ok ) class ( sqpopt_dense_ldl_type ), intent ( inout ) :: me real ( wp ), dimension (:), intent ( inout ) :: v !! the right-hand side, overwritten by the solution logical , intent ( out ) :: ok !! whether it was solved integer :: i , j real ( wp ) :: s , t do i = 1 , me % n if ( me % piv ( i ) /= i ) then t = v ( i ) v ( i ) = v ( me % piv ( i )) v ( me % piv ( i )) = t end if end do do i = 2 , me % n s = v ( i ) do j = 1 , i - 1 s = s - me % lu ( i , j ) * v ( j ) end do v ( i ) = s end do do i = me % n , 1 , - 1 s = v ( i ) do j = i + 1 , me % n s = s - me % lu ( i , j ) * v ( j ) end do v ( i ) = s / me % lu ( i , i ) end do ok = sqpopt_all_finite ( v ) end subroutine dense_back_solve","tags":"","url":"proc/dense_back_solve.html"},{"title":"dense_multiply – sqpopt","text":"private  subroutine dense_multiply(me, x, y) the product with the values last factored. Type Bound sqpopt_dense_ldl_type Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( sqpopt_dense_ldl_type ), intent(in) :: me real(kind=wp), intent(in), dimension(:) :: x the vector dimension(n) real(kind=wp), intent(out), dimension(:) :: y the product dimension(n) Source Code subroutine dense_multiply ( me , x , y ) class ( sqpopt_dense_ldl_type ), intent ( in ) :: me real ( wp ), dimension (:), intent ( in ) :: x !! the vector `dimension(n)` real ( wp ), dimension (:), intent ( out ) :: y !! the product `dimension(n)` integer :: i , j do i = 1 , me % n y ( i ) = 0.0_wp end do do j = 1 , me % n do i = 1 , me % n y ( i ) = y ( i ) + me % a ( i , j ) * x ( j ) end do end do end subroutine dense_multiply","tags":"","url":"proc/dense_multiply.html"},{"title":"dense_free – sqpopt","text":"private  subroutine dense_free(me) free everything. Type Bound sqpopt_dense_ldl_type Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( sqpopt_dense_ldl_type ), intent(inout) :: me Source Code subroutine dense_free ( me ) class ( sqpopt_dense_ldl_type ), intent ( inout ) :: me if ( allocated ( me % a )) deallocate ( me % a ) if ( allocated ( me % lu )) deallocate ( me % lu ) if ( allocated ( me % piv )) deallocate ( me % piv ) if ( allocated ( me % irow )) deallocate ( me % irow ) if ( allocated ( me % icol )) deallocate ( me % icol ) me % n = 0 end subroutine dense_free","tags":"","url":"proc/dense_free.html"},{"title":"filter_step_acceptable – sqpopt","text":"private  function filter_step_acceptable(me, theta_k, phi_k, gtp, alpha, theta_t, phi_t, f_type) result(ok) whether a trial point with violation theta_t and objective phi_t ,\nreached with step length alpha from the current point\n( theta_k , phi_k ), is acceptable (see filter_line_search for the\nrules). gtp is the predicted change in the objective along the full\nstep ( for the line search; the trust region passes the\nquadratic model's , with alpha=1 ). f_type is set if the\nswitching condition held (so the step was judged on the objective alone,\nand must not enlarge the filter). The trial point must also be\nacceptable to the filter itself: , and not\ndominated by any filter entry ( or for every entry j ). Type Bound sqpopt_filter_type Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( sqpopt_filter_type ), intent(in) :: me real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: theta_k violation and objective at the current point real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: phi_k violation and objective at the current point real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: gtp predicted change in the objective along the full step real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: alpha step length real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: theta_t violation and objective at the trial point real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: phi_t violation and objective at the trial point logical, intent(out) :: f_type true if the switching condition held Return Value logical Calls proc~~filter_step_acceptable~~CallsGraph proc~filter_step_acceptable sqpopt_filter_type%filter_step_acceptable proc~merit_slack merit_slack proc~filter_step_acceptable->proc~merit_slack Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Called by proc~~filter_step_acceptable~~