( theta_k ) end if if ( f_type ) then ! Armijo condition on the objective (with a roundoff-level slack): ok = phi_t <= phi_k + me % eta_phi * alpha * gtp + merit_slack ( phi_k ) else ! sufficient reduction of the violation or the objective: ok = theta_t <= ( 1.0_wp - me % gamma_theta ) * theta_k . or . & phi_t <= phi_k - me % gamma_phi * theta_k end if if (. not . ok ) return ! acceptable to the filter: ok = theta_t < me % theta_max if (. not . ok ) return do j = 1 , size ( me % theta ) if ( theta_t >= me % theta ( j ) . and . phi_t >= me % phi ( j )) then ok = . false . return end if end do end function filter_step_acceptable","tags":"","url":"proc/filter_step_acceptable.html"},{"title":"filter_min_step – sqpopt","text":"private pure function filter_min_step(me, theta_k, gtp) result(alpha_min) Wächter & Biegler's minimum step length : below it,\nno trial step can be acceptable (so the line search should give up and\ngo to feasibility restoration). Type Bound sqpopt_filter_type Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( sqpopt_filter_type ), intent(in) :: me real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: theta_k violation at the current point real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: gtp Return Value real(kind=wp) Called by proc~~filter_min_step~~CalledByGraph proc~filter_min_step sqpopt_filter_type%filter_min_step proc~filter_line_search filter_line_search proc~filter_line_search->proc~filter_min_step proc~line_search sqpopt_linesearch_type%line_search proc~line_search->proc~filter_line_search proc~sqpopt_iterate sqpopt_iterate proc~sqpopt_iterate->proc~line_search proc~sqpopt_solve sqpopt_type%sqpopt_solve proc~sqpopt_solve->proc~sqpopt_iterate proc~nlls_solve sqpopt_nlls_type%nlls_solve proc~nlls_solve->proc~sqpopt_solve Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code pure function filter_min_step ( me , theta_k , gtp ) result ( alpha_min ) class ( sqpopt_filter_type ), intent ( in ) :: me real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: theta_k !! violation at the current point real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: gtp !!  g&#94;Tp  real ( wp ) :: alpha_min if ( gtp < 0.0_wp ) then alpha_min = min ( me % gamma_theta , me % gamma_phi * theta_k / ( - gtp )) if ( theta_k <= me % theta_min ) then if ( theta_k > 0.0_wp ) then alpha_min = min ( alpha_min , exp ( log ( me % delta ) + me % s_theta * log ( theta_k ) & - me % s_phi * log ( - gtp ))) else alpha_min = 0.0_wp end if end if else alpha_min = me % gamma_theta end if alpha_min = me % gamma_alpha * alpha_min end function filter_min_step","tags":"","url":"proc/filter_min_step.html"},{"title":"filter_point_acceptable – sqpopt","text":"private  function filter_point_acceptable(me, theta, phi) result(ok) whether a point with violation theta and objective phi is acceptable\nto the filter: , and not dominated by any\nfilter entry (always true before the filter is initialized). Type Bound sqpopt_filter_type Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( sqpopt_filter_type ), intent(in) :: me real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: theta constraint violation real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: phi objective Return Value logical Called by proc~~filter_point_acceptable~~CalledByGraph proc~filter_point_acceptable sqpopt_filter_type%filter_point_acceptable proc~point_acceptable sqpopt_linesearch_type%point_acceptable proc~point_acceptable->proc~filter_point_acceptable proc~restoration_phase_done sqpopt_restoration_type%restoration_phase_done proc~restoration_phase_done->proc~point_acceptable proc~sqpopt_iterate sqpopt_iterate