e to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine filter_augment ( me , theta_k , phi_k ) class ( sqpopt_filter_type ), intent ( inout ) :: me real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: theta_k , phi_k !! violation and objective at the current point real ( wp ) :: theta_new , phi_new logical , dimension (:), allocatable :: keep if (. not . me % ready ) call me % prepare ( theta_k ) theta_new = ( 1.0_wp - me % gamma_theta ) * theta_k phi_new = phi_k - me % gamma_phi * theta_k if ( size ( me % theta ) > 0 ) then keep = . not . ( me % theta >= theta_new . and . me % phi >= phi_new ) me % theta = pack ( me % theta , keep ) me % phi = pack ( me % phi , keep ) end if me % theta = [ me % theta , theta_new ] me % phi = [ me % phi , phi_new ] end subroutine filter_augment","tags":"","url":"proc/filter_augment.html"},{"title":"diagnostics_problem_report – sqpopt","text":"private  function diagnostics_problem_report(me) result(text) the report on the starting point made by diagnostics_start (empty\nbelow level 2 ), for the header of the printed output. Type Bound sqpopt_diagnostics_type Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( sqpopt_diagnostics_type ), intent(in) :: me Return Value character(len=:), allocatable Called by proc~~diagnostics_problem_report~~CalledByGraph proc~diagnostics_problem_report sqpopt_diagnostics_type%diagnostics_problem_report proc~sqpopt_solve sqpopt_type%sqpopt_solve proc~sqpopt_solve->proc~diagnostics_problem_report proc~nlls_solve sqpopt_nlls_type%nlls_solve proc~nlls_solve->proc~sqpopt_solve Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a 