ame – sqpopt","text":"public pure function sqpopt_linear_solver_name(solver) result(name) the name of the sparse solver solver (a sqpopt_linear_solver_* value). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: solver the solver ( sqpopt_linear_solver_* ) Return Value character(len=:), allocatable Called by proc~~sqpopt_linear_solver_name~~CalledByGraph proc~sqpopt_linear_solver_name sqpopt_linear_solver_name proc~sqpopt_solve sqpopt_type%sqpopt_solve proc~sqpopt_solve->proc~sqpopt_linear_solver_name proc~nlls_solve sqpopt_nlls_type%nlls_solve proc~nlls_solve->proc~sqpopt_solve Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code pure function sqpopt_linear_solver_name ( solver ) result ( name ) integer , intent ( in ) :: solver !! the solver (`sqpopt_linear_solver_*`) character ( len = :), allocatable :: name select case ( solver ) case ( sqpopt_linear_solver_mumps ) name = 'MUMPS' case ( sqpopt_linear_solver_dense ) name = 'dense' case default name = 'QDLDL' end select end function sqpopt_linear_solver_name","tags":"","url":"proc/sqpopt_linear_solver_name.html"},{"title":"symmetric_solver_initialize – sqpopt","text":"private  subroutine symmetric_solver_initialize(me, n, irow, icol, ok, threads, solver, signs) start the solver for symmetric matrices of order n with the sparsity\npattern irow / icol : each entry stands for itself and (off the\ndiagonal) its mirror image, so give each off-diagonal element in one\ntriangle only; entries given more than once are added together. solver is the backend (a sqpopt_linear_solver_* value; default\nQDLDL). threads is the number of OpenMP threads to factor and solve\nwith (MUMPS only; see sqpopt_mumps_ldl_module ; default 1). signs is the expected sign of each row's pivot (QDLDL only): -1 for the rows\nof a block that should be negative definite (the constraints of a KKT\nmatrix), else +1 or 0 (see delay_negative_rows ). ok is false\nif the solver isn't available in this build, or couldn't be started. Type Bound sqpopt_symmetric_solver_type Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( sqpopt_symmetric_solver_type ), intent(inout) :: me integer, intent(in) :: n order of the matrix integer, intent(in), dimension(:) :: irow row indices of the entries dimension(nnz) integer, intent(in), dimension(:) :: icol column indices of the entries dimension(nnz) logical, intent(out) :: ok whether the solver is ready integer, intent(in), optional :: threads number of OpenMP threads (default 1 ; 0 : as the OpenMP\nenvironment says) integer, intent(in), optional :: solver the sparse solver ( sqpopt_linear_solver_* , default QDLDL) integer, intent(in), optional, dimension(:) :: signs the expected sign of each row's pivot dimension(n) (see above) Calls proc~~symmetric_solver_initialize~~CallsGraph proc~symmetric_solver_initialize sqpopt_symmetric_solver_type%symmetric_solver_initialize proc~sqpopt_linear_solver_available sqpopt_linear_solver_available proc~symmetric_solver_initialize->proc~sqpopt_linear_solver_available proc~symmetric_solver_destroy sqpopt_symmetric_solver_type%symmetric_solver_destroy proc~symmetric_solver_initialize->proc~symmetric_solver_destroy start start proc~symmetric_solver_initialize->start Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Called by proc~~symmetric_solver_initialize~~CalledByGraph proc~symmetric_solver_initialize sqpopt_symmetric_solver_type%symmetric_solver_initialize proc~kkt_initialize sqpopt_kkt_type%kkt_initialize proc~kkt_initialize->proc~symmetric_solver_initialize proc~least_squares_initialize sqpopt_least_squares_type%least_squares_initialize proc~least_squares_initialize->proc~kkt_initialize Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine symmetric_solver_initialize ( me , n , irow , icol , ok , threads , solver , signs ) class ( sqpopt_symmetric_solver_type ), intent ( inout ) :: me integer , intent ( in ) :: n !! order of the matrix integer , dimension (:), intent ( in ) :: irow !! row indices of the entries `dimension(nnz)` integer , dimension (:), intent ( in ) :: icol !! column indices of the entries `dimension(nnz)` logical , intent ( out ) :: ok !! whether the solver is ready integer , optional , intent ( in ) :: threads !! number of OpenMP threads (default `1`; `0`: as the OpenMP !! environment says) integer , optional , intent ( in ) :: solver !! the sparse solver (`sqpopt_linear_solver_*`, default QDLDL) integer , dimension (:), optional , intent ( in ) :: signs !! the expected sign of each row's pivot `dimension(n)` !! (see above) integer :: which , alloc_stat call me % destroy () ok = . false . which = sqpopt_linear_solver_qdldl if ( present ( solver )) which = solver if (. not . sqpopt_linear_solver_available ( which )) return select case ( which ) case ( sqpopt_linear_solver_mumps ) allocate ( sqpopt_mumps_ldl_type :: me % ldl , stat = alloc_stat ) case ( sqpopt_linear_solver_dense ) allocate ( sqpopt_dense_ldl_type :: me % ldl , stat = alloc_stat ) case default allocate ( sqpopt_qdldl_ldl_type :: me % ldl , stat = alloc_stat ) end select if ( alloc_stat /= 0 ) then me % out_of_memory = . true . return end if call me % ldl % start ( n , irow , icol , ok , threads = threads , signs = signs ) if (. not . ok ) then me % out_of_memory = me % ldl % out_of_memory call me % ldl % free () deallocate ( me % ldl ) return end if me % n = n me % backend = which me % ready = . true . end subroutine symmetric_solver_initialize","tags":"","url":"proc/symmetric_solver_initialize.html"},{"title":"symmetric_solver_factor – sqpopt","text":"private  subroutine symmetric_solver_factor(me, val, ok) factor the matrix with the values val (in the order of the pattern\ngiven to symmetric_solver_initialize ). On success, n_negative , n_null , and inertia_known describe its inertia (see the module\ndocumentation), and symmetric_solver_solve can be called. Type Bound sqpopt_symmetric_solver_type Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( sqpopt_symmetric_solver_type ), intent(inout) :: me real(kind=wp), intent(in), dimension(:) :: val values of the entries dimension(nnz) logical, intent(out) :: ok whether the factorization succeeded Calls proc~~symmetric_solver_factor~~CallsGraph proc~symmetric_solver_factor sqpopt_symmetric_solver_type%symmetric_solver_factor refactor refactor proc~symmetric_solver_factor->refactor Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Called by proc~~symmetric_solver_factor~~CalledByGraph proc~symmetric_solver_factor sqpopt_symmetric_solver_type%symmetric_solver_factor proc~factor_values factor_values proc~factor_values->proc~symmetric_solver_factor proc~kkt_factor sqpopt_kkt_type%kkt_factor proc~kkt_factor->proc~factor_values proc~kkt_factor_identity sqpopt_kkt_type%kkt_factor_identity proc~kkt_factor_identity->proc~factor_values proc~direct_qp_step direct_qp_step proc~direct_qp_step->proc~kkt_factor proc~inertia_correct sqpopt_inertia_type%inertia_correct proc~direct_qp_step->proc~inertia_correct proc~inertia_correct->proc~kkt_factor proc~least_squares_min_norm sqpopt_least_squares_type%least_squares_min_norm proc~least_squares_min_norm->proc~kkt_factor_identity proc~least_squares_multipliers sqpopt_least_squares_type%least_squares_multipliers proc~least_squares_multipliers->proc~kkt_factor_identity proc~multiplier_estimate multiplier_estimate proc~multiplier_estimate->proc~least_squares_multipliers proc~restoration_step restoration_step proc~restoration_step->proc~least_squares_min_norm proc~soc_step soc_step proc~soc_step->proc~least_squares_min_norm proc~solve_qp_subproblem sqpopt_qp_solver_type%solve_qp_subproblem proc~solve_qp_subproblem->proc~direct_qp_step proc~sqpopt_iterate sqpopt_iterate proc~sqpopt_iterate->proc~inertia_correct proc~sqpopt_iterate->proc~multiplier_estimate proc~sqpopt_iterate->proc~restoration_step proc~sqpopt_iterate->proc~solve_qp_subproblem proc~restoration_phase_step sqpopt_restoration_type%restoration_p