)) if (. not . rnorm_new <= 0.5_wp * rnorm ) exit b = x_new rnorm = rnorm_new end do end if if ( ok ) ok = sqpopt_all_finite ( b ) call system_clock ( t1 ) me % time = me % time + real ( t1 - t0 , wp ) / real ( rate , wp ) contains subroutine back_solve ( v , success ) !! one solve with the factors: `v` is overwritten by  A&#94;{-1} v  real ( wp ), dimension (:), intent ( inout ) :: v !! the right-hand side, overwritten by the solution logical , intent ( out ) :: success !! whether it was solved (if not, `v` is unchanged) me % n_solve = me % n_solve + 1 call me % ldl % back_solve ( v , success ) if ( me % ldl % out_of_memory ) me % out_of_memory = . true . end subroutine back_solve end subroutine symmetric_solver_solve","tags":"","url":"proc/symmetric_solver_solve.html"},{"title":"symmetric_solver_multiply – sqpopt","text":"private  subroutine symmetric_solver_multiply(me, x, y) the product with the matrix last given to symmetric_solver_factor (used for the residuals of the refinement,\nand for testing). Type Bound sqpopt_symmetric_solver_type Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( sqpopt_symmetric_solver_type ), intent(in) :: me real(kind=wp), intent(in), dimension(:) :: x the vector dimension(n) real(kind=wp), intent(out), dimension(:) :: y the product dimension(n) Calls proc~~symmetric_solver_multiply~~CallsGraph proc~symmetric_solver_multiply sqpopt_symmetric_solver_type%symmetric_solver_multiply multiply multiply proc~symmetric_solver_multiply->multiply Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimple