y Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Called by proc~~least_squares_min_norm~~CalledByGraph proc~least_squares_min_norm sqpopt_least_squares_type%least_squares_min_norm proc~restoration_step restoration_step proc~restoration_step->proc~least_squares_min_norm proc~soc_step soc_step proc~soc_step->proc~least_squares_min_norm proc~sqpopt_iterate sqpopt_iterate proc~sqpopt_iterate->proc~restoration_step proc~trust_region_step sqpopt_trust_region_type%trust_region_step proc~sqpopt_iterate->proc~trust_region_step proc~trust_region_step->proc~soc_step proc~sqpopt_solve sqpopt_type%sqpopt_solve proc~sqpopt_solve->proc~sqpopt_iterate proc~nlls_solve sqpopt_nlls_type%nlls_solve proc~nlls_solve->proc~sqpopt_solve Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine least_squares_min_norm ( me , jac , rows , r , d , ok ) class ( sqpopt_least_squares_type ), intent ( inout ) :: me type ( sqpopt_sparse_matrix ), intent ( in ) :: jac !! the constraint Jacobian `dimension(m,n)` logical , dimension (:), intent ( in ) :: rows !! whether each row is in `S` `dimension(m)` real ( wp ), dimension (:), intent ( in ) :: r !! the right-hand side (used for the rows in `S`) `dimension(m)` real ( wp ), dimension (:), intent ( out ) :: d !! the solution `dimension(n)` logical , intent ( out ) :: ok !! whether `d` was computed integer , dimension (:), allocatable :: status real ( wp ), dimension (:), allocatable :: v allocate ( status ( me % m + me % n ), v ( me % n + me % m )) d = 0.0_wp ok = . false . if (. not . me % enabled ) return ! (the working set is the rows of `S`, and no variable is fixed) status = 0 where ( rows ) status ( 1 : me % m ) = 1 call me % kkt % factor_identity ( 1.0_wp , jac , status , regularization ( jac , rows ), ok ) if ( ok ) then v ( 1 : me % n ) = 0.0_wp v ( me % n + 1 :) = merge ( r , 0.0_wp , rows ) call me % kkt % solve ( v , ok ) if ( ok ) ok = sqpopt_all_finite ( v ( 1 : me % n )) end if if (. not . ok ) then me % enabled = . false . return end if d = v ( 1 : me % n ) end subroutine least_squares_min_norm","tags":"","url":"proc/least_squares_min_norm.html"},{"title":"least_squares_multipliers – sqpopt","text":"private  subroutine least_squares_multipliers(me, jac, rows, free, g, lambda, ok) the (regularized) least-squares multipliers of the rows S of jac selected by rows , in the variables selected by free : , from the system\nof the module documentation with the right-hand side . lambda is only set for the rows in S . ok is false if the solver\nisn't enabled, or the factorization or the solve failed (the solver is\nthen disabled for the rest of the solve). Type Bound sqpopt_least_squares_type Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( sqpopt_least_squares_type ), intent(inout) :: me type( sqpopt_sparse_matrix ), intent(in) :: jac the constraint Jacobian dimension(m,n) logical, intent(in), dimension(:) :: rows whether each row is in S dimension(m) logical, intent(in), dimension(:) :: free whether each variable is free (not at a bound) dimension(n) real(kind=wp), intent(in), dimension(:) :: g the objective gradient dimension(n) real(kind=wp), intent(inout), dimension(:) :: lambda the multipliers dimension(m) (set for the rows in S ) logical, intent(out) :: ok whether they were computed Calls proc~~least_squares_multipliers~~CallsGraph proc~least_squares_multipliers sqpopt_least_squares_type%least_squares_multipliers proc~kkt_factor_identity sqpopt_kkt_type%kkt_factor_identity proc~least_squares_multipliers->proc~kkt_factor_identity proc~kkt_solve sqpopt_kkt_type%kkt_solve proc~least_squares_multipliers->proc~kkt_solve proc~regularization regularization proc~least_squares_multipliers->proc~regularization proc~sqpopt_all_finite sqpopt_all_finite proc~least_squares_multipliers->proc~sqpopt_all_finite proc~factor_values factor_values proc~kkt_factor_identity->proc~factor_values proc~dense_lu_solve dense_lu_solve proc~kkt_solve->proc~dense_lu_solve proc~hessian_low_rank_multiply sqpopt_hessian_type%hessian_low_rank_multiply proc~kkt_solve->proc~hessian_low_rank_multiply proc~hessian_low_rank_multiply_transpose sqpopt_hessian_type%hessian_low_rank_multiply_transpose proc~kkt_solve->proc~hessian_low_rank_multiply_transpose proc~symmetric_solver_solve sqpopt_symmetric_solver_type%symmetric_solver_solve proc~kkt_solve->proc~symmetric_solver_solve proc~kkt_negatives kkt_negatives proc~factor_values->proc~kkt_negatives proc~symmetric_solver_factor sqpopt_symmetric_solver_type%symmetric_solver_factor proc~factor_values->proc~symmetric_solver_factor proc~pair_col pair_col proc~hessian_low_rank_multiply->proc~pair_col proc~hessian_low_rank_multiply_transpose->proc~pair_col proc~symmetric_solver_solve->proc~sqpopt_all_finite back_solve back_solve proc~symmetric_solver_solve->back_solve proc~symmetric_solver_multiply sqpopt_symmetric_solver_type%symmetric_solver_multiply proc~symmetric_solver_solve->proc~symmetric_solver_multiply refactor refactor proc~symmetric_solver_factor->refactor multiply multiply proc~symmetric_solver_multiply->multiply Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Called by proc~~least_squares_multipliers~~CalledByGraph proc~least_squares_multipliers sqpopt_least_squares_type%least_squares_multipliers proc~multiplier_estimate multiplier_estimate proc~multiplier_estimate->proc~least_squares_multipliers proc~sqpopt_iterate sqpopt_iterate proc~sqpopt_iterate->proc~multiplier_estimate proc~sqpopt_solve sqpopt_type%sqpopt_solve proc~sqpopt_solve->proc~sqpopt_iterate proc~nlls_solve sqpopt_nlls_type%nlls_solve proc~nlls_solve->proc~sqpopt_solve Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine least_squares_multipliers ( me , jac , rows , free , g , lambda , ok ) class ( sqpopt_least_squares_type ), intent ( inout ) :: me type ( sqpopt_sparse_matrix ), intent ( in ) :: jac !! the constraint Jacobian `dimension(m,n)` logical , dimension (:), intent ( in ) :: rows !! whether each row is in `S` `dimension(m)` logical , dimension (:), intent ( in ) :: free !! whether each variable is free (not at a bound) `dimension(n)` real ( wp ), dimension (:), intent ( in ) :: g !! the objective gradient `dimension(n)` real ( wp ), dimension (:), intent ( inout ) :: lambda !! the multipliers `dimension(m)` (set for the rows in `S`) logical , intent ( out ) :: ok !! whether they were computed integer , dimension (:), allocatable :: status real ( wp ), dimension (:), allocatable :: v allocate ( status ( me % m + me % n ), v ( me % n + me % m )) ok = . false . if (. not . me % enabled ) return ! (the working set is the rows of `S`, and the variables that are not free) status = 0 where ( rows ) status ( 1 : me % m ) = 1 where (. not . free ) status ( me % m + 1 :) = 1 call me % kkt % factor_identity ( 1.0_wp , jac , status , regularization ( jac , rows , free ), ok ) if ( ok ) then v ( 1 : me % n ) = merge ( g , 0.0_wp , free ) v ( me % n + 1 :) = 0.0_wp call me % kkt % solve ( v , ok ) if ( ok ) ok = sqpopt_all_finite ( v ( me % n + 1 :)) end if if (. not . ok ) then me % enabled = . false . return end if where ( rows ) lambda = v ( me % n + 1 :) end subroutine least_squares_multipliers","tags":"","url":"proc/least_squares_multipliers.html"},{"title":"multiplier_estimate – sqpopt","text":"public  subroutine multiplier_estimate(jac, rows, free, g, lambda, ok, least_squares) a first-order estimate of the constraint multipliers at a point: the\nleast-squares solution of the stationarity condition over the rows S of jac selected by rows , in the variables selected\nby free (those not at a bound, whose bound multipliers are not zero).\nUnlike the multipliers of a QP subproblem, it doesn't depend on the QP's\nHessian. lambda is only set for the rows in S , and only if ok . It is computed by the direct solver least_squares , if that is given\nand enabled (see options%direct_least_squares ), and otherwise by the\niterative solver LSQR ; ok is false if that stops at its iteration\nlimit. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( sqpopt_sparse_matrix ), intent(in) :: jac the constraint Jacobian dimension(m,n) logical, intent(in), dimension(:) :: rows whether each row is in S dimension(m) logical, intent(in), dimension(:) :: free whether each variable is free (not at a bound) dimension(n) real(kind=wp), intent(in), dimension(:) :: g the objective gradient dimension(n) real(kind=wp), intent(inout), dimension(:) :: lambda the multipliers dimension(m) (set for the rows in S ) logical, intent(out) :: ok whether they were computed type( sqpopt_least_squares_type ), intent(inout), optional :: least_squares the direct least-squares solver Calls proc~~multiplier_estimate~~CallsGraph proc~multiplier_estimate multiplier_estimate initialize initialize proc~multiplier_estimate->initialize proc~least_squares_multipliers sqpopt_least_squares_type%least_squares_multipliers proc~multiplier_estimate->proc~least_squares_multipliers proc~sqpopt_all_finite sqpopt_all_finite proc~multiplier_estimate->proc~sqpopt_all_finite solve solve proc~multiplier_estimate->solve proc~least_squares_multipliers->proc~sqpopt_all_finite proc~kkt_factor_identity sqpopt_kkt_type%kkt_factor_identity proc~least_squares_multipliers->proc~kkt_factor_identity proc~kkt_solve sqpopt_kkt_type%kkt_solve proc~least_squares_multipliers->proc~kkt_solve proc~regularization regularization proc~least_squares_multipliers->proc~regularization proc~factor_values factor_values proc~kkt_factor_identity->proc~factor_values proc~dense_lu_solve dense_lu_solve proc~kkt_solve->proc~dense_lu_solve proc~hessian_low_rank_multiply sqpopt_hessian_type%hessian_low_rank_multiply proc~kkt_solve->proc~hessian_low_rank_multiply proc~hessian_low_rank_multiply_transpose sqpopt_hessian_type%hessian_low_rank_multiply_transpose proc~kkt_solve->proc~hessian_low_rank_multiply_transpose proc~symmetric_solver_solve sqpopt_symmetric_solver_type%symmetric_solver_solve proc~kkt_solve->proc~symmetric_solver_solve proc~kkt_negatives kkt_negatives proc~factor_values->proc~kkt_negatives proc~symmetric_solver_factor sqpopt_symmetric_solver_type%symmetric_solver_factor proc~factor_values->proc~symmetric_solver_factor proc~pair_col pair_col proc~hessian_low_rank_multiply->proc~pair_col proc~hessian_low_rank_multiply_transpose->proc~pair_col proc~symmetric_solver_solve->proc~sqpopt_all_finite back_solve back_solve proc~symmetric_solver_solve->back_solve proc~symmetric_solver_multiply sqpopt_symmetric_solver_type%symmetric_solver_multiply proc~symmetric_solver_solve->proc~symmetric_solver_multiply refactor refactor proc~symmetric_solver_factor->refactor multiply multiply proc~symmetric_solver_multiply->multiply Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Called by proc~~multiplier_estimate~~CalledByGraph proc~multiplier_estimate multiplier_estimate proc~sqpopt_iterate sqpopt_iterate proc~sqpopt_iterate->proc~multiplier_estimate proc~sqpopt_solve sqpopt_type%sqpopt_solve proc~sqpopt_solve->proc~sqpopt_iterate proc~nlls_solve sqpopt_nlls_type%nlls_solve proc~nlls_solve->proc~sqpopt_solve Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine multiplier_estimate ( jac , rows , free , g , lambda , ok , least_squares ) type ( sqpopt_sparse_matrix ), intent ( in ) :: jac !! the constraint Jacobian `dimension(m,n)` logical , dimension (:), intent ( in ) :: rows !! whether each row is in `S` `dimension(m)` logical , dimension (:), intent ( in ) :: free !! whether each variable is free (not at a bound) `dimension(n)` real ( wp ), dimension (:), intent ( in ) :: g !! the objective gradient `dimension(n)` real ( wp ), dimension (:), intent ( inout ) :: lambda !! the multipliers `dimension(m)` (set for the rows in `S`) logical , intent ( out ) :: ok !! whether they were computed type ( sqpopt_least_squares_type ), optional , intent ( inout ) :: least_squares !! the direct least-squares solver integer , parameter :: lsqr_itnlim_stop = 5 !! `LSQR`'s `istop` for \"iteration limit reached\" type ( lsqr_solver_ez ) :: lsqr integer , dimension (:), allocatable :: irow , icol , col_of_row real ( wp ), dimension (:), allocatable :: val , lam , rhs integer :: m , n , m_s , nnz_s , i , k , istop m = size ( rows ) n = size ( free ) ok = . false . m_s = count ( rows ) if ( m_s == 0 ) return if ( present ( least_squares )) then call least_squares % multipliers ( jac , rows , free , g , lambda , ok ) if ( ok ) return end if ! the transposed sub-Jacobian (free variables x rows of S), for LSQR: allocate ( col_of_row ( m )) col_of_row = 0 k = 0 do i = 1 , m if ( rows ( i )) then k = k + 1 col_of_row ( i ) = k end if end do allocate ( irow ( jac % nnz ), icol ( jac % nnz ), val ( jac % nnz ), lam ( m_s )) nnz_s = 0 do k = 1 , jac % nnz if ( rows ( jac % irow ( k )) . and . free ( jac % icol ( k ))) then nnz_s = nnz_s + 1 irow ( nnz_s ) = jac % icol ( k ) icol ( nnz_s ) = col_of_row ( jac % irow ( k )) val ( nnz_s ) = jac % val ( k ) end if end do call lsqr % initialize ( n , m_s , val ( 1 : nnz_s ), irow ( 1 : nnz_s ), icol ( 1 : nnz_s ), itnlim = 4 * ( m_s + n ) + 10 ) allocate ( rhs ( n )) rhs = merge ( g , 0.0_wp , free ) call lsqr % solve ( rhs , 0.0_wp , lam , istop ) if ( istop == lsqr_itnlim_stop . or . . not . sqpopt_all_finite ( lam )) return do i = 1 , m if ( rows ( i )) lambda ( i ) = lam ( col_of_row ( i )) end do ok = . true . end subroutine multiplier_estimate","tags":"","url":"proc/multiplier_estimate.html"},{"title":"least_squares_destroy – sqpopt","text":"private  subroutine least_squares_destroy(me) free the solver, and return to the initial (disabled) state. It does\nnothing if the solver was never started. Type Bound sqpopt_least_squares_type Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( sqpopt_least_squares_type ), intent(inout) :: me Calls proc~~least_squares_destroy~~CallsGraph proc~least_squares_destroy sqpopt_least_squares_type%least_squares_destroy proc~kkt_destroy sqpopt_kkt_type%kkt_destroy proc~least_squares_destroy->proc~kkt_destroy proc~symmetric_solver_destroy sqpopt_symmetric_solver_type%symmetric_solver_destroy proc~kkt_destroy->proc~symmetric_solver_destroy Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine least_squares_destroy ( me ) class ( sqpopt_least_squares_type ), intent ( inout ) :: me call me % kkt % destroy () me % enabled = . false . me % n = 0 me % m = 0 end subroutine least_squares_destroy","tags":"","url":"proc/least_squares_destroy.html"},{"title":"mumps_start – sqpopt","text":"private  subroutine mumps_start(me, n, irow, icol, ok, threads, signs) start MUMPS for the pattern (it is analysed in the first factorization). ok is false if the library was built without MUMPS, or MUMPS couldn't\nbe started. signs is not used (MUMPS pivots). Type Bound sqpopt_mumps_ldl_type Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( sqpopt_mumps_ldl_type ), intent(inout) :: me integer, intent(in) :: n order of the matrix integer, intent(in), dimension(:) :: irow row indices of the entries dimension(nnz) integer, intent(in), dimension(:) :: icol column indices of the entries dimension(nnz) logical, intent(out) :: ok whether the backend is ready integer, intent(in), optional :: threads number of OpenMP threads (default 1 ; 0 : as the OpenMP\nenvironment says) integer, intent(in), optional, dimension(:) :: signs (not used) Source Code subroutine mumps_start ( me , n , irow , icol , ok , threads , signs ) class ( sqpopt_mumps_ldl_type ), intent ( inout ) :: me integer , intent ( in ) :: n !! order of the matrix integer , dimension (:), intent ( in ) :: irow !! row indices of the entries `dimension(nnz)` integer , dimension (:), intent ( in ) :: icol !! column indices of the entries `dimension(nnz)` logical , intent ( out ) :: ok !! whether the backend is ready integer , optional , intent ( in ) :: threads !! number of OpenMP threads (default `1`; `0`: as the OpenMP !! environment says) integer , dimension (:), optional , intent ( in ) :: signs !! (not used) #ifdef HAS_MUMPS integer :: nnz , alloc_stat #endif ok = . false . if ( present ( signs )) continue ! (MUMPS pivots) #ifdef HAS_MUMPS nnz = size ( irow ) allocate ( me % id , stat = alloc_stat ) if ( alloc_stat /= 0 ) then nullify ( me % id ) me % out_of_memory = . true . return end if me % id % comm = 0 ! (the sequential library's MPI is a stub: no communicator is needed) me % id % sym = 2 ! general symmetric me % id % par = 1 me % id % job = - 1 call dmumps ( me % id ) if ( me % id % infog ( 1 ) < 0 ) then deallocate ( me % id ) return end if me % id % icntl ( 1 : 3 ) = - 1 ! no printed output me % id % icntl ( 4 ) = 0 me % id % icntl ( 13 ) = 1 ! (needed for the number of negative pivots to be exact) me % id % icntl ( 16 ) = 1 ! the number of OpenMP threads (see the module documentation) if ( present ( threads )) me % id % icntl ( 16 ) = max ( threads , 0 ) me % id % icntl ( 24 ) = 1 ! detect null pivots, rather than fail on a singular matrix me % id % n = n me % id % nnz = int ( nnz , kind ( me % id % nnz )) allocate ( me % id % irn ( nnz ), stat = alloc_stat ) if ( alloc_stat == 0 ) allocate ( me % id % jcn ( nnz ), stat = alloc_stat ) if ( alloc_stat == 0 ) allocate ( me % id % a ( nnz ), stat = alloc_stat ) if ( alloc_stat == 0 ) allocate ( me % id % rhs ( n ), stat = alloc_stat ) if ( alloc_stat /= 0 ) then call me % free () me % out_of_memory = . true . return end if me % id % irn = irow me % id % jcn = icol ok = . true . #endif end subroutine mumps_start","tags":"","url":"proc/mumps_start.html"},{"title":"mumps_refactor – sqpopt","text":"private  subroutine mumps_refactor(me, val, ok) factor the matrix with the values val . The pattern is analysed in the\nfirst call, with that call's values. If MUMPS runs out of its estimated\nworkspace, the factorization is repeated with twice the allowance, up\nto 20 times (as IPOPT does), and the larger allowance is kept for the\nfollowing factorizations. Type Bound sqpopt_mumps_ldl_type Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( sqpopt_mumps_ldl_type ), intent(inout) :: me real(kind=wp), intent(in), dimension(:) :: val values of the entries dimension(nnz) logical, intent(out) :: ok whether the factorization succeeded Source Code subroutine mumps_refactor ( me , val , ok ) class ( sqpopt_mumps_ldl_type ), intent ( inout ) :: me real ( wp ), dimension (:), intent ( in ) :: val !! values of the entries `dimension(nnz)` logical , intent ( out ) :: ok !! whether the factorization succeeded #ifdef HAS_MUMPS integer :: attempt integer , parameter :: max_attempts = 20 !! (each doubles the workspace increase; a very indefinite matrix, !! whose pivots are delayed, can need many times the estimate) #endif ok = . false . me % inertia_known = . true . #ifdef HAS_MUMPS me % id % a = val do attempt = 1 , max_attempts me % id % job = merge ( 2 , 4 , me % analysed ) ! (4: analyse, then factor) call dmumps ( me % id ) if ( me % id % infog ( 1 ) /= - 8 . and . me % id % infog ( 1 ) /= - 9 ) exit me % id % icntl ( 14 ) = 2 * max ( me % id % icntl ( 14 ), 20 ) ! more workspace (a percentage of the estimate) end do if ( me % id % infog ( 1 ) < 0 ) then ! (-13: an allocation failed; -5, -7: an allocation of the analysis failed; ! -8, -9: still not enough workspace) if ( any ( me % id % infog ( 1 ) == [ - 13 , - 5 , - 7 , - 8 , - 9 ])) me % out_of_memory = . true . return end if me % analysed = . true . me % n_negative = me % id % infog ( 12 ) me % n_null = me % id % infog ( 28 ) ok = . true . #endif end subroutine mumps_refactor","tags":"","url":"proc/mumps_refactor.html"},{"title":"mumps_back_solve – sqpopt","text":"private  subroutine mumps_back_solve(me, v, ok) one solve with the factors, without refinement. Type Bound sqpopt_mumps_ldl_type Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( sqpopt_mumps_ldl_type ), intent(inout) :: me real(kind=wp), intent(inout), dimension(:) :: v the right-hand side, overwritten by the solution logical, intent(out) :: ok whether it was solved Source Code subroutine mumps_back_solve ( me , v , ok ) class ( sqpopt_mumps_ldl_type ), intent ( inout ) :: me real ( wp ), dimension (:), intent ( inout ) :: v !! the right-hand side, overwritten by the solution logical , intent ( out ) :: ok !! whether it was solved ok = . false . #ifdef HAS_MUMPS me % id % rhs = v me % id % job = 3 call dmumps ( me % id ) ok = me % id % infog ( 1 ) >= 0 if ( ok ) then v = me % id % rhs else if ( me % id % infog ( 1 ) == - 13 ) then me % out_of_memory = . true . ! (an allocation failed) end if #endif end subroutine mumps_back_solve","tags":"","url":"proc/mumps_back_solve.html"},{"title":"mumps_multiply – sqpopt","text":"private  subroutine mumps_multiply(me, x, y) the product with the values last factored. Type Bound sqpopt_mumps_ldl_type Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( sqpopt_mumps_ldl_type ), intent(in) :: me real(kind=wp), intent(in), dimension(:) :: x the vector dimension(n) real(kind=wp), intent(out), dimension(:) :: y the product dimension(n) Source Code subroutine mumps_multiply ( me , x , y ) class ( sqpopt_mumps_ldl_type ), intent ( in ) :: me real ( wp ), dimension (:), intent ( in ) :: x !! the vector `dimension(n)` real ( wp ), dimension (:), intent ( out ) :: y !! the product `dimension(n)` #ifdef HAS_MUMPS integer :: k , i , j #endif y = 0.0_wp #ifdef HAS_MUMPS if (. not . associated ( me % id )) return do k = 1 , size ( me % id % a ) i = me % id % irn ( k ) j = me % id % jcn ( k ) y ( i ) = y ( i ) + me % id % a ( k ) * x ( j ) if ( i /= j ) y ( j ) = y ( j ) + me % id % a ( k ) * x ( i ) end do #endif end subroutine mumps_multiply","tags":"","url":"proc/mumps_multiply.html"},{"title":"mumps_free – sqpopt","text":"private  subroutine mumps_free(me) free everything (it does nothing if MUMPS was never started). Type Bound sqpopt_mumps_ldl_type Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( sqpopt_mumps_ldl_type ), intent(inout) :: me Source Code subroutine mumps_free ( me ) class ( sqpopt_mumps_ldl_type ), intent ( inout ) :: me #ifdef HAS_MUMPS if ( associated ( me % id )) then if ( associated ( me % id % irn )) deallocate ( me % id % irn ) if ( associated ( me % id % jcn )) deallocate ( me % id % jcn ) if ( associated ( me % id % a )) deallocate ( me % id % a ) if ( associated ( me % id % rhs )) deallocate ( me % id % rhs ) me % id % job = - 2 call dmumps ( me % id ) deallocate ( me % id ) end if #endif me % analysed = . false . end subroutine mumps_free","tags":"","url":"proc/mumps_free.html"},{"title":"log_on – sqpopt","text":"private pure function log_on(me, level) whether messages of the given level are printed. Type Bound sqpopt_log_type Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( sqpopt_log_type ), intent(in) :: me integer, intent(in) :: level the print_level a message needs Return Value logical Called by proc~~log_on~~CalledByGraph proc~log_on sqpopt_log_type%log_on proc~log_merit_trial log_merit_trial proc~log_merit_trial->proc~log_on proc~log_theta_trial log_theta_trial proc~log_theta_trial->proc~log_on proc~sqpopt_iterate sqpopt_iterate proc~sqpopt_iterate->proc~log_on proc~trust_region_step sqpopt_trust_region_type%trust_region_step proc~sqpopt_iterate->proc~trust_region_step proc~line_search sqpopt_linesearch_type%line_search proc~sqpopt_iterate->proc~line_search proc~trust_region_step->proc~log_on proc~backtrack_search backtrack_search proc~backtrack_search->proc~log_merit_trial proc~filter_line_search filter_line_search proc~filter_line_search->proc~log_theta_trial proc~funnel_line_search funnel_line_search proc~funnel_line_search->proc~log_theta_trial proc~sqpopt_solve sqpopt_type%sqpopt_solve proc~sqpopt_solve->proc~sqpopt_iterate proc~armijo_line_search armijo_line_search proc~armijo_line_search->proc~backtrack_search proc~line_search->proc~filter_line_search proc~line_search->proc~funnel_line_search proc~line_search->proc~armijo_line_search proc~watchdog_line_search watchdog_line_search proc~line_search->proc~watchdog_line_search proc~nlls_solve sqpopt_nlls_type%nlls_solve proc~nlls_solve->proc~sqpopt_solve proc~watchdog_line_search->proc~backtrack_search Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows