n ) :: x !! the number character ( len = :), allocatable :: s character ( len = 32 ) :: buf integer :: ios write ( buf , '(ES16.9)' , iostat = ios ) x if ( ios /= 0 ) then s = '****' else s = trim ( adjustl ( buf )) end if end function fmt_g","tags":"","url":"proc/fmt_g.html"},{"title":"fmt_i – sqpopt","text":"public pure function fmt_i(i) result(s) an integer, without padding. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: i the number Return Value character(len=:), allocatable Called by proc~~fmt_i~~CalledByGraph proc~fmt_i fmt_i proc~diagnostics_finish sqpopt_diagnostics_type%diagnostics_finish proc~diagnostics_finish->proc~fmt_i proc~plural plural proc~diagnostics_finish->proc~plural proc~diagnostics_record sqpopt_diagnostics_type%diagnostics_record proc~diagnostics_record->proc~fmt_i proc~diagnostics_start sqpopt_diagnostics_type%diagnostics_start proc~diagnostics_start->proc~fmt_i proc~listed listed proc~diagnostics_start->proc~listed proc~diagnostics_start->proc~plural proc~listed->proc~fmt_i proc~plural->proc~fmt_i proc~qp_status_text qp_status_text proc~qp_status_text->proc~fmt_i proc~sqpopt_iterate sqpopt_iterate proc~sqpopt_iterate->proc~fmt_i proc~sqpopt_iterate->proc~plural proc~sqpopt_iterate->proc~qp_status_text proc~trust_region_step sqpopt_trust_region_type%trust_region_step proc~sqpopt_iterate->proc~trust_region_step proc~sqpopt_solve sqpopt_type%sqpopt_solve proc~sqpopt_solve->proc~fmt_i proc~sqpopt_solve->proc~diagnostics_finish proc~sqpopt_solve->proc~diagnostics_record proc~sqpopt_solve->proc~diagnostics_start proc~sqpopt_solve->proc~plural proc~sqpopt_solve->proc~sqpopt_iterate proc~nlls_solve sqpopt_nlls_type%nlls_solve proc~nlls_solve->proc~sqpopt_solve proc~trust_region_step->proc~qp_status_text Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code pure function fmt_i ( i ) result ( s ) integer , intent ( in ) :: i !! the number character ( len = :), allocatable :: s character ( len = 32 ) :: buf integer :: ios write ( buf , '(I0)' , iostat = ios ) i if ( ios /= 0 ) then s = '****' else s = trim ( adjustl ( buf )) end if end function fmt_i","tags":"","url":"proc/fmt_i.html"},{"title":"qp_status_text – sqpopt","text":"public pure function qp_status_text(istat) result(s) a short description of a QP solve's status, for the log. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: istat the QP solve's status code (see sqpopt_types_module ) Return Value character(len=:), allocatable Calls proc~~qp_status_text~~CallsGraph proc~qp_status_text qp_status_text proc~fmt_i fmt_i proc~qp_status_text->proc~fmt_i Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Called by proc~~qp_status_text~~CalledByGraph proc~qp_status_text qp_status_text proc~sqpopt_iterate sqpopt_iterate proc~sqpopt_iterate->proc~qp_status_text proc~trust_region_step sqpopt_trust_region_type%trust_region_step proc~sqpopt_iterate->proc~trust_region_step proc~trust_region_step->proc~qp_status_