outine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine log_put ( me , level , line ) class ( sqpopt_log_type ), intent ( in ) :: me integer , intent ( in ) :: level !! the `print_level` the line needs character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: line !! the text (without the indentation, which is added) integer :: ios ! (a failed write, e.g. to a unit that isn't open, is ignored: the log ! must never stop the solver) if ( me % level >= level ) write ( me % unit , '(A)' , iostat = ios ) '        . ' // line end subroutine log_put","tags":"","url":"proc/log_put.html"},{"title":"initial_step_length – sqpopt","text":"private  function initial_step_length(x, p, step_limit) result(alpha0) the initial trial step length used by every line search mode before any\nbacktracking (SNOPT's \"Major step limit\" option): i.e. p is scaled down (never up) so that no variable changes by more\nthan a factor of step_limit relative to . Returns 1 unchanged if p is zero. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(in), dimension(:) :: x current point and search direction, dimension(n) real(kind=wp), intent(in), dimension(:) :: p current point and search direction, dimension(n) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: step_limit sqpopt_linesearch_type%major_step_limit Return Value real(kind=wp) initial trial step length Called by proc~~initial_step_length~~CalledByGraph proc~initial_step_length initial_step_length proc~armijo_line_search armijo_line_search proc~armijo_line_search->proc~initial_step_length proc~exact_line_search exact_line_search proc~exact_line_search->proc~initial_step_length proc~filter_line_search filter_line_search proc~filter_line_search->proc~initial_step_length proc~funnel_line_search funnel_line_search proc~funnel_line_search->proc~initial_step_length proc~watchdog_line_search watchdog_line_search proc~watchdog_line_search->proc~initial_step_length proc~line_search sqpopt_linesearch_type%line_search proc~line_search->proc~armijo_line_search proc~line_search->proc~exact_line_search proc~line_search->proc~filter_line_search proc~line_search->proc~funnel_line_search proc~line_search->proc~watchdog_line_search proc~sqpopt_iterate sqpopt_iterate proc~sqpopt_iterate->proc~line_search proc~sqpopt_solve sqpopt_type%sqpopt_solve proc~sqpopt_solve->proc~sqpopt_iterate proc~nlls_solve sqpopt_nlls_type%nlls_solve proc~nlls_solve->proc~sqpopt_solve Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code function initial_step_length ( x , p , step_limit ) result ( alpha0 ) real ( wp ), dimension (:), intent ( in ) :: x , p !! current point and search direction, `dimension(n)` real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: step_limit !! `sqpopt_linesearch_type%major_step_limit` real ( wp ) :: alpha0 !! initial trial step length real ( wp ) :: rmax integer :: k rmax = 0.0_wp do k = 1 , size ( x ) rmax = max ( rmax , abs ( p ( k )) / max ( 1.0_wp , abs ( x ( k )))) end do ! (written so that `step_limit=huge(1.0_wp)` can't overflow) if ( rmax > step_limit ) then alpha0 = step_limit / rmax else alpha0 = 1.0_wp end if end function initial_step_length","tags":"","url":"proc/initial_step_length.html"},{"title":"next_step_length – sqpopt","text":"private pure function next_step_length(me, alpha, phi0, dphi0, phi_a) result(alpha_new) the next trial step length after alpha was rejected: backtrack*alpha ,\nor, if interpolate , the minimizer of the quadratic interpolating , , and (as in NLPQLP), safeguarded to (and backtrack*alpha if the\nquadratic has no minimizer, e.g. ). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( sqpopt_linesearch_type ), intent(in) :: me real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: alpha the rejected step length real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: phi0 real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dphi0 real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: phi_a Return Value real(kind=wp) Called by proc~~next_step_length~~CalledByGraph proc~next_step_length next_step_length proc~backtrack_search backtrack_search proc~backtrack_search->proc~next_step_length proc~filter_line_search filter_line_search proc~filter_line_search->proc~next_step_length proc~funnel_line_search funnel_line_search proc~funnel_line_search->proc~next_step_length proc~armijo_line_search armijo_line_search proc~armijo_line_search->proc~backtrack_search proc~line_search sqpopt_linesearch_type%line_search proc~line_search->proc~filter_line_search proc~line_search->proc~funnel_line_search proc~line_search->proc~armijo_line_search proc~watchdog_line_search watchdog_line_search proc~line_search->proc~watchdog_line_search proc~watchdog_line_search->proc~backtrack_search proc~sqpopt_iterate sqpopt_iterate proc~sqpopt_iterate->proc~line_search proc~sqpopt_solve sqpopt_type%sqpopt_solve proc~sqpopt_solve->proc~sqpopt_iterate proc~nlls_solve sqpopt_nlls_type%nlls_solve proc~nlls_solve->proc~sqpopt_solve Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code pure function next_step_length ( me , alpha , phi0 , dphi0 , phi_a ) result ( alpha_new ) class ( sqpopt_linesearch_type ), intent ( in ) :: me real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: alpha !! the rejected step length real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: phi0 !!  \\phi(0)  real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: dphi0 !!  \\phi'(0)  real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: phi_a !!  \\phi(\\alpha)  real ( wp ) :: alpha_new real ( wp ) :: curv alpha_new = me % backtrack * alpha if (. not . me % interpolate . or . dphi0 >= 0.0_wp ) return curv = phi_a - phi0 - alpha * dphi0 if ( curv <= 0.0_wp ) return alpha_new = min ( max ( - 0.5_wp * alpha ** 2 * dphi0 / curv , 0.1_wp * alpha ), 0.5_wp * alpha ) end function next_step_length","tags":"","url":"proc/next_step_length.html"},{"title":"point_acceptable – sqpopt","text":"private  function point_acceptable(me, theta, phi) result(ok) whether a point with violation theta and objective phi is acceptable\nto the filter ( sqpopt_linesearch_filter mode) or to the funnel\n( sqpopt_linesearch_funnel mode); always true in the other modes. Used\nto decide when a feasibility restoration phase can end (see sqpopt_restoration_module ). Type Bound sqpopt_linesearch_type Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( sqpopt_linesearch_type ), intent(in) :: me real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: theta constraint violation real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: phi objective Return Value logical Calls proc~~point_acceptable~~CallsGraph proc~point_acceptable sqpopt_linesearch_type%point_acceptable proc~filter_point_acceptable sqpopt_filter_type%filter_point_acceptable proc~point_acceptable->proc~filter_point_acceptable Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Called by proc~~point_acceptable~~CalledByGraph proc~point_acceptable sqpopt_linesearch_type%point_acceptable proc~restoration_phase_done sqpopt_restoration_type%restoration_phase_done proc~restoration_phase_done->proc~point_acceptable proc~sqpopt_iterate sqpopt_iterate proc~sqpopt_iterate->proc~restoration_phase_done proc~sqpopt_solve sqpopt_type%sqpopt_solve proc~sqpopt_solve->proc~sqpopt_iterate proc~nlls_solve sqpopt_nlls_type%nlls_solve proc~nlls_solve->proc~sqpopt_solve Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code function point_acceptable ( me , theta , phi ) result ( ok ) class ( sqpopt_linesearch_type ), intent ( in ) :: me real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: theta !! constraint violation real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: phi !! objective logical :: ok select case ( me % mode ) case ( sqpopt_linesearch_filter ) ok = me % filter % acceptable ( theta , phi ) case ( sqpopt_linesearch_funnel ) ok = me % funnel % acceptable ( theta ) case default ok = . true . end select end function point_acceptable","tags":"","url":"proc/point_acceptable.html"},{"title":"line_search – sqpopt","text":"private  subroutine line_search(me, eval_f, eval_c, x, p, f, g, c, jac, lambda, c_lb, c_ub, alpha, x_new, istat, soc) perform a line search along the direction p to find an accepted step\nlength alpha , dispatching to the strategy selected by me%mode . If no acceptable step is found, istat=sqpopt_line_search_failed and x_new=x (no step is taken; in sqpopt_linesearch_watchdog mode a\nfailed relaxed window instead returns the best point found so far).\nTrial points where f or c is not finite (NaN or Inf) are always\nrejected, so the search backtracks away from them. If soc is present, a second-order correction of the first trial\nstep is also tried when that step is rejected and did not reduce the\nconstraint violation (see sqpopt_soc_module ); in sqpopt_linesearch_exact mode, when the minimizer along p falls\nshort of the full step and the full step did not reduce the violation. Type Bound sqpopt_linesearch_type Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( sqpopt_linesearch_type ), intent(inout) :: me procedure( sqpopt_ls_objective_func ) :: eval_f evaluates procedure( sqpopt_ls_constraint_func ) :: eval_c evaluates real(kind=wp), intent(in), dimension(:) :: x current point dimension(n) real(kind=wp), intent(in), dimension(:) :: p search direction dimension(n) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: f objective function value at x real(kind=wp), intent(in), dimension(:) :: g objective gradient at x dimension(n) real(kind=wp), intent(in), dimension(:) :: c constraint values at x dimension(m) type( sqpopt_sparse_matrix ), intent(in) :: jac constraint Jacobian at x , dimension(m,n) (only used by sqpopt_merit_augmented_lagrangian ) real(kind=wp), intent(in), dimension(:) :: lambda Lagrange multiplier estimate dimension(m) (only used by sqpopt_merit_augmented_lagrangian ) real(kind=wp), intent(in), dimension(:) :: c_lb constraint lower bounds dimension(m) real(kind=wp), intent(in), dimension(:) :: c_ub constraint upper bounds dimension(m) real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: alpha accepted step length ( 0 if no step was taken) real(kind=wp), intent(out), dimension(:) :: x_new the accepted new point dimension(n) (normally x + alpha*p ; see above for the exceptions) integer, intent(out) :: istat status code (see sqpopt_types_module ) procedure( sqpopt_soc_func ), optional :: soc computes a second-order-corrected step Calls proc~~line_search~~CallsGraph proc~line_search sqpopt_linesearch_type%line_search proc~armijo_line_search armijo_line_search proc~line_search->proc~armijo_line_search proc~exact_line_search exact_line_search proc~line_search->proc~exact_line_search proc~filter_line_search filter_line_search proc~line_search->proc~filter_line_search proc~funnel_line_search funnel_line_search proc~line_search->proc~funnel_line_search proc~watchdog_line_search watchdog_line_search proc~line_search->proc~watchdog_line_search proc~backtrack_search backtrack_search proc~armijo_line_search->proc~backtrack_search proc~eval_merit_function sqpopt_merit_type%eval_merit_function proc~armijo_line_search->proc~eval_merit_function proc~fmt_g fmt_g proc~armijo_line_search->proc~fmt_g proc~initial_step_length initial_step_length proc~armijo_line_search->proc~initial_step_length proc~log_put sqpopt_log_type%log_put proc~armijo_line_search->proc~log_put proc~merit_directional_derivative sqpopt_merit_type%merit_directional_derivative proc~armijo_line_search->proc~merit_directional_derivative proc~nonmonotone_push nonmonotone_push proc~armijo_line_search->proc~nonmonotone_push fmin fmin proc~exact_line_search->fmin proc~exact_line_search->proc~eval_merit_function proc~eval_trial eval_trial proc~exact_line_search->proc~eval_trial proc~fmt_e fmt_e proc~exact_line_search->proc~fmt_e proc~exact_line_search->proc~fmt_g proc~exact_line_search->proc~initial_step_length proc~l1_violation l1_violation proc~exact_line_search->proc