Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Called by proc~~kkt_factor~~CalledByGraph proc~kkt_factor sqpopt_kkt_type%kkt_factor proc~direct_qp_step direct_qp_step proc~direct_qp_step->proc~kkt_factor proc~inertia_correct sqpopt_inertia_type%inertia_correct proc~direct_qp_step->proc~inertia_correct proc~inertia_correct->proc~kkt_factor proc~solve_qp_subproblem sqpopt_qp_solver_type%solve_qp_subproblem proc~solve_qp_subproblem->proc~direct_qp_step proc~sqpopt_iterate sqpopt_iterate proc~sqpopt_iterate->proc~inertia_correct proc~sqpopt_iterate->proc~solve_qp_subproblem proc~restoration_phase_step sqpopt_restoration_type%restoration_phase_step proc~sqpopt_iterate->proc~restoration_phase_step proc~trust_region_step sqpopt_trust_region_type%trust_region_step proc~sqpopt_iterate->proc~trust_region_step proc~restoration_phase_step->proc~solve_qp_subproblem proc~sqpopt_solve sqpopt_type%sqpopt_solve proc~sqpopt_solve->proc~sqpopt_iterate proc~trust_region_step->proc~solve_qp_subproblem proc~nlls_solve sqpopt_nlls_type%nlls_solve proc~nlls_solve->proc~sqpopt_solve Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine kkt_factor ( me , hessian , jac , status , ok , reg ) class ( sqpopt_kkt_type ), intent ( inout ) :: me type ( sqpopt_hessian_type ), intent ( inout ) :: hessian !! the Hessian (see [[sqpopt_hessian_module]]) type ( sqpopt_sparse_matrix ), intent ( in ) :: jac !! the constraint Jacobian `dimension(m,n)` integer , dimension (:), intent ( in ) :: status !! the working set: nonzero for each general row, then each !! variable bound, that is in it `dimension(m+n)` logical , intent ( out ) :: ok !! whether the factorization is available real ( wp ), optional , intent ( in ) :: reg !! the regularization  \\epsilon \\ge 0  (default 0) real ( wp ) :: eps real ( wp ), dimension ( 0 ) :: no_values logical :: kept eps = 0.0_wp if ( present ( reg )) eps = reg if ( hessian % exact ) then call factor_values ( me , hessian % shift , hessian % h_val , jac , status , eps , ok ) else call factor_values ( me , 1.0_wp / hessian % gamma + hessian % shift , no_values , jac , status , eps , ok , kept ) if ( ok . and . . not . kept ) call low_rank_update ( me , hessian , ok ) end if end subroutine kkt_factor","tags":"","url":"proc/kkt_factor.html"},{"title":"kkt_factor_identity – sqpopt","text":"private  subroutine kkt_factor_identity(me, scale, jac, status, reg, ok) factor the KKT matrix of the working set status with the Hessian scale and the regularization reg ( ),\nas kkt_factor does for the exact Hessian. The matrix must have been\ninitialized without a Hessian pattern. Type Bound sqpopt_kkt_type Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( sqpopt_kkt_type ), intent(inout) :: me real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: scale the Hessian is scale times the identity type( sqpopt_sparse_matrix ), intent(in) :: jac the constraint Jacobian dimension(m,n) integer, intent(in), dimension(:) :: status the working set (see kkt_factor ) dimension(m+n) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: reg the regularization logical, intent(out) :: ok whether the factorization is available Calls proc~~kkt_factor_identity~~CallsGraph proc~kkt_factor_identity sqpopt_kkt_type%kkt_factor_identity proc~factor_values factor_values proc~kkt_factor_identity->proc~factor_values proc~kkt_negatives kkt_negatives proc~factor_values->proc~kkt_negatives proc~symmetric_solver_factor sqpopt_symmetric_solver_type%symmetric_solver_factor proc~factor_values->proc~symmetric_solver_factor refactor refactor proc~symmetric_solver_factor->refactor Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Called by proc~~kkt_factor_identity~~CalledByGraph proc~kkt_factor_identity sqpopt_kkt_type%kkt_factor_identity proc~least_squares_min_norm sqpopt_least_squares_type%least_squares_min_norm proc~least_squares_min_norm->proc~kkt_factor_identity proc~least_squares_multipliers sqpopt_least_squares_type%least_squares_multipliers proc~least_squares_multipliers->proc~kkt_factor_identity proc~multiplier_estimate multiplier_estimate proc~multiplier_estimate->proc~least_squares_multipliers proc~restoration_step restoration_step proc~restoration_step->proc~least_squares_min_norm proc~soc_step soc_step proc~soc_step->proc~least_squares_min_norm proc~sqpopt_iterate sqpopt_iterate proc~sqpopt_iterate->proc~multiplier_estimate proc~sqpopt_iterate->proc~restoration_step proc~trust_region_step sqpopt_trust_region_type%trust_region_step proc~sqpopt_iterate->proc~trust_region_step proc~trust_region_step->proc~soc_step proc~sqpopt_solve sqpopt_type%sqpopt_solve proc~sqpopt_solve->proc~sqpopt_iterate proc~nlls_solve sqpopt_nlls_type%nlls_solve proc~nlls_solve->proc~sqpopt_solve Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine kkt_factor_identity ( me , scale , jac , status , reg , ok ) class ( sqpopt_kkt_type ), intent ( inout ) :: me real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: scale !! the Hessian is `scale` times the identity type ( sqpopt_sparse_matrix ), intent ( in ) :: jac !! the constraint Jacobian `dimension(m,n)` integer , dimension (:), intent ( in ) :: status !! the working set (see [[kkt_factor]]) `dimension(m+n)` real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: reg !! the regularization  \\epsilon \\ge 0  logical , intent ( out ) :: ok !! whether the factorization is available real ( wp ), dimension ( 0 ) :: no_values call factor_values ( me , scale , no_values , jac , status , reg , ok ) end subroutine kkt_factor_identity","tags":"","url":"proc/kkt_factor_identity.html"},{"title":"factor_values – sqpopt","text":"private  subroutine factor_values(me, diag, h_val, jac, status, reg, ok, kept) assemble and factor (see the module documentation) for the\nHessian with the values h_val (in the pattern given to kkt_initialize ) plus diag on its diagonal, unless that is the\nfactorization that is kept ( kept ). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( sqpopt_kkt_type ), intent(inout) :: me real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: diag added to the Hessian's diagonal real(kind=wp), intent(in), dimension(:) :: h_val the Hessian's values, in its pattern's order type( sqpopt_sparse_matrix ), intent(in) :: jac the constraint Jacobian dimension(m,n) integer, intent(in), dimension(:) :: status the working set (see kkt_factor ) dimension(m+n) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: reg the regularization logical, intent(out) :: ok whether the factorization is available logical, intent(out), optional :: kept whether it is the one that was kept (nothing was computed) Calls proc~~factor_values~~CallsGraph proc~factor_values factor_values proc~kkt_negatives kkt_negatives proc~factor_values->proc~kkt_negatives proc~symmetric_solver_factor sqpopt_symmetric_solver_type%symmetric_solver_factor proc~factor_values->proc~symmetric_solver_factor refactor refactor proc~symmetric_solver_factor->refactor Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Called by proc~~factor_values~~CalledByGraph proc~factor_values factor_values proc~kkt_factor sqpopt_kkt_type%kkt_factor proc~kkt_factor->proc~factor_values proc~kkt_factor_identity sqpopt_kkt_type%kkt_factor_identity proc~kkt_factor_identity->proc~factor_values proc~direct_qp_step direct_qp_step proc~direct_qp_step->proc~kkt_factor proc~inertia_correct sqpopt_inertia_type%inertia_correct proc~direct_qp_step->proc~inertia_correct proc~inertia_correct->proc~kkt_factor proc~least_squares_min_norm sqpopt_least_squares_type%least_squares_min_norm proc~least_squares_min_norm->proc~kkt_factor_identity proc~least_squares_multipliers sqpopt_least_squares_type%least_squares_multipliers proc~least_squares_multipliers->proc~kkt_factor_identity proc~multiplier_estimate multiplier_estimate proc~multiplier_estimate->proc~least_squares_multipliers proc~restoration_step restoration_step proc~restoration_step->proc~least_squares_min_norm proc~soc_step soc_step proc~soc_step->proc~least_squares_min_norm proc~solve_qp_subproblem sqpopt_qp_solver_type%solve_qp_subproblem proc~solve_qp_subproblem->proc~direct_qp_step proc~sqpopt_iterate sqpopt_iterate proc~sqpopt_iterate->proc~inertia_correct proc~sqpopt_iterate->proc~multiplier_estimate proc~sqpopt_iterate->proc~restoration_step proc~sqpopt_iterate->proc~solve_qp_subproblem proc~restoration_phase_step sqpopt_restoration_type%restoration_phase_step proc~sqpopt_iterate->proc~restoration_phase_step proc~trust_region_step sqpopt_trust_region_type%trust_region_step proc~sqpopt_iterate->proc~trust_region_step proc~restoration_phase_step->proc~solve_qp_subproblem proc~sqpopt_solve sqpopt_type%sqpopt_solve proc~sqpopt_solve->proc~sqpopt_iterate proc~trust_region_step->proc~soc_step proc~trust_region_step->proc~solve_qp_subproblem proc~nlls_solve sqpopt_nlls_type%nlls_solve proc~nlls_solve->proc~sqpopt_solve Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine factor_values ( me , diag , h_val , jac , status , reg , ok , kept ) class ( sqpopt_kkt_type ), intent ( inout ) :: me real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: diag !! added to the Hessian's diagonal real ( wp ), dimension (:), intent ( in ) :: h_val !! the Hessian's values, in its pattern's order type ( sqpopt_sparse_matrix ), intent ( in ) :: jac !! the constraint Jacobian `dimension(m,n)` integer , dimension (:), intent ( in ) :: status !! the working set (see [[kkt_factor]]) `dimension(m+n)` real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: reg !! the regularization  \\epsilon \\ge 0  logical , intent ( out ) :: ok !! whether the factorization is available logical , optional , intent ( out ) :: kept !! whether it is the one that was kept (nothing was computed) integer :: n , m , nh , k , i , j ok = . false . if ( present ( kept )) kept = . false . if (. not . me % enabled ) return if ( me % current ) then if ( diag == me % diag . and . reg == me % reg . and . all (( status /= 0 ) . eqv . me % in_set )) then ok = . true . if ( present ( kept )) kept = . true . return end if end if n = me % n m = me % m nh = size ( me % h_irow ) ! the diagonal: `diag`, or 1 for a variable at a bound of the working ! set; and `-reg`, or -1 for a constraint outside it: do j = 1 , n me % val ( j ) = merge ( 1.0_wp , diag , status ( m + j ) /= 0 ) end do do i = 1 , m me % val ( n + i ) = merge ( - reg , - 1.0_wp , status ( i ) /= 0 ) end do ! the Hessian's elements between free variables: do k = 1 , nh i = me % h_irow ( k ) j = me % h_icol ( k ) me % val ( n + m + k ) = merge ( 0.0_wp , h_val ( k ), status ( m + i ) /= 0 . or . status ( m + j ) /= 0 ) end do ! the Jacobian's elements of the working set's rows, in the free variables: do k = 1 , jac % nnz me % val ( n + m + nh + k ) = merge ( jac % val ( k ), 0.0_wp , status ( jac % irow ( k )) /= 0 . and . status ( m + jac % icol ( k )) == 0 ) end do me % current = . false . call me % solver % factor ( me % val , ok ) if (. not . ok ) then ! (fall back on the matrix-free methods from here on) me % enabled = . false . return end if me % inertia_known = me % solver % inertia_known me % n_negative = max ( kkt_negatives ( me ) - m , 0 ) me % singular = me % solver % inertia_known . and . me % solver % n_null > 0 me % current = . true . me % in_set = status /= 0 me % diag = diag me % reg = reg me % rank = 0 end subroutine factor_values","tags":"","url":"proc/factor_values.html"},{"title":"low_rank_update – sqpopt","text":"private  subroutine low_rank_update(me, hessian, ok) complete the factorization of just made for the quasi-Newton\nHessian hessian (see the module documentation): form the matrix (one solve with for each of its r columns) and\nits LU factorization, and correct n_negative and singular for the\nlow-rank part. (A BFGS matrix is positive definite, so its face has no\nnegative curvature, and the inertias are only computed for SR1.) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( sqpopt_kkt_type ), intent(inout) :: me type( sqpopt_hessian_type ), intent(inout) :: hessian the quasi-Newton Hessian logical, intent(out) :: ok whether the solves succeeded Calls proc~~low_rank_update~~CallsGraph proc~low_rank_update low_rank_update proc~dense_lu_factor dense_lu_factor proc~low_rank_update->proc~dense_lu_factor proc~dense_symmetric_inertia dense_symmetric_inertia proc~low_rank_update->proc~dense_symmetric_inertia proc~hessian_low_rank_column sqpopt_hessian_type%hessian_low_rank_column proc~low_rank_update->proc~hessian_low_rank_column proc~hessian_low_rank_middle sqpopt_hessian_type%hessian_low_rank_middle proc~low_rank_update->proc~hessian_low_rank_middle proc~hessian_low_rank_multiply_transpose sqpopt_hessian_type%hessian_low_rank_multiply_transpose proc~low_rank_update->proc~hessian_low_rank_multiply_transpose proc~hessian_low_rank_size sqpopt_hessian_type%hessian_low_rank_size proc~low_rank_update->proc~hessian_low_rank_size proc~kkt_negatives kkt_negatives proc~low_rank_update->proc~kkt_negatives proc~symmetric_solver_solve sqpopt_symmetric_solver_type%symmetric_solver_solve proc~low_rank_update->proc~symmetric_solver_solve proc~pair_col pair_col proc~hessian_low_rank_column->proc~pair_col proc~middle_matrix middle_matrix proc~hessian_low_rank_middle->proc~middle_matrix proc~hessian_low_rank_multiply_transpose->proc~pair_col proc~factor_middle_matrix factor_middle_matrix proc~hessian_low_rank_size->proc~factor_middle_matrix back_solve back_solve proc~symmetric_solver_solve->back_solve proc~sqpopt_all_finite sqpopt_all_finite proc~symmetric_solver_solve->proc~sqpopt_all_finite proc~symmetric_solver_multiply sqpopt_symmetric_solver_type%symmetric_solver_multiply proc~symmetric_solver_solve->proc~symmetric_solver_multiply proc~factor_middle_matrix->proc~dense_lu_factor proc~factor_middle_matrix->proc~middle_matrix proc~middle_matrix->proc~pair_col multiply multiply proc~symmetric_solver_multiply->multiply Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Called by proc~~low_rank_update~~CalledByGraph proc~low_rank_update low_rank_update proc~kkt_factor sqpopt_kkt_type%kkt_factor proc~kkt_factor->proc~low_rank_update proc~direct_qp_step direct_qp_step proc~direct_qp_step->proc~kkt_factor proc~inertia_correct sqpopt_inertia_type%inertia_correct proc~direct_qp_step->proc~inertia_correct proc~inertia_correct->proc~kkt_factor proc~solve_qp_subproblem sqpopt_qp_solver_type%solve_qp_subproblem proc~solve_qp_subproblem->proc~direct_qp_step proc~sqpopt_iterate sqpopt_iterate proc~sqpopt_iterate->proc~inertia_correct proc~sqpopt_iterate->proc~solve_qp_subproblem proc~restoration_phase_step sqpopt_restoration_type%restoration_phase_step proc~sqpopt_iterate->proc~restoration_phase_step proc~trust_region_step sqpopt_trust_region_type%trust_region_step proc~sqpopt_iterate->proc~trust_region_step proc~restoration_phase_step->proc~solve_qp_subproblem proc~sqpopt_solve sqpopt_type%sqpopt_solve proc~sqpopt_solve->proc~sqpopt_iterate proc~trust_region_step->proc~solve_qp_subproblem proc~nlls_solve sqpopt_nlls_type%nlls_solve proc~nlls_solve->proc~sqpopt_solve Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine low_rank_update ( me , hessian , ok ) class ( sqpopt_kkt_type ), intent ( inout ) :: me type ( sqpopt_hessian_type ), intent ( inout ) :: hessian !! the quasi-Newton Hessian logical , intent ( out ) :: ok !! whether the solves succeeded real ( wp ), dimension (:,:), allocatable :: t , sm real ( wp ), dimension (:), allocatable :: v real ( wp ) :: sigma integer :: r , j , n , pos_t , pos_m , n_neg , n_zero logical :: nonsingular allocate ( v ( me % n + me % m )) ok = . true . n = me % n r = hessian % low_rank_size () me % rank = r if ( r == 0 ) return allocate ( t ( r , r ), sm ( r , r )) call hessian % low_rank_middle ( sm , sigma ) sm = sigma * sm ! T = sigma*M + E&#94;T K0&#94;{-1} E, a column at a time: do j = 1 , r call hessian % low_rank_column ( j , v ( 1 : n )) where ( me % in_set ( me % m + 1 :)) v ( 1 : n ) = 0.0_wp v ( n + 1 :) = 0.0_wp call me % solver % solve ( v , ok , refine = . false .) if (. not . ok ) then me % enabled = . false . me % current = . false . return end if where ( me % in_set ( me % m + 1 :)) v ( 1 : n ) = 0.0_wp call hessian % low_rank_multiply_transpose ( v ( 1 : n ), t (:, j )) end do t = sm + 0.5_wp * ( t + transpose ( t )) ! the inertia of K, from those of K0, T, and sigma*M: if ( sigma > 0.0_wp ) then call dense_symmetric_inertia ( sm , pos_m , n_neg , n_zero ) call dense_symmetric_inertia ( t , pos_t , n_neg , n_zero ) me % n_negative = max ( kkt_negatives ( me ) + pos_t - pos_m - me % m , 0 ) end if if ( allocated ( me % t_lu )) deallocate ( me % t_lu , me % t_piv ) allocate ( me % t_piv ( r )) call move_alloc ( t , me % t_lu ) call dense_lu_factor ( me % t_lu , me % t_piv , nonsingular ) if (. not . nonsingular ) me % singular = . true . end subroutine low_rank_update","tags":"","url":"proc/low_rank_update.html"},{"title":"kkt_solve – sqpopt","text":"private  subroutine kkt_solve(me, v, ok, hessian) solve with the factorization that is kept: v holds r on entry and the solution on exit. Its first n elements belong to the\nvariables, and the other m to the constraints. Because of the fixed\npattern (see the module documentation), the solution's element is the\nright-hand side's own for a variable at a bound of the working set, and\nminus that for a constraint outside it. hessian must be given if the factorization was made for a\nquasi-Newton Hessian (the same one): its low-rank part is then applied\nby the Sherman-Morrison-Woodbury formula (see the module documentation). ok is false if there is no factorization, or no finite solution. Type Bound sqpopt_kkt_type Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( sqpopt_kkt_type ), intent(inout) :: me real(kind=wp), intent(inout), dimension(:) :: v the right-hand side, overwritten by the solution dimension(n+m) logical, intent(out) :: ok whether a solution was found type( sqpopt_hessian_type ), intent(in), optional :: hessian the quasi-Newton Hessian that was factored Calls proc~~kkt_solve~~CallsGraph proc~kkt_solve sqpopt_kkt_type%kkt_solve proc~dense_lu_solve dense_lu_solve proc~kkt_solve->proc~dense_lu_solve proc~hessian_low_rank_multiply sqpopt_hessian_type%hessian_low_rank_multiply proc~kkt_solve->proc~hessian_low_rank_multiply proc~hessian_low_rank_multiply_transpose sqpopt_hessian_type%hessian_low_rank_multiply_transpose proc~kkt_solve->proc~hessian_low_rank_multiply_transpose proc~symmetric_solver_solve sqpopt_symmetric_solver_type%symmetric_solver_solve proc~kkt_solve->proc~symmetric_solver_solve proc~pair_col pair_col proc~hessian_low_rank_multiply->proc~pair_col proc~hessian_low_rank_multiply_transpose->proc~pair_col back_solve back_solve proc~symmetric_solver_solve->back_solve proc~sqpopt_all_finite sqpopt_all_finite proc~symmetric_solver_solve->proc~sqpopt_all_finite proc~symmetric_solver_multiply sqpopt_symmetric_solver_type%symmetric_solver_multiply proc~symmetric_solver_solve->proc~symmetric_solver_multiply multiply multiply proc~symmetric_solver_multiply->multiply Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Called by proc~~kkt_solve~~CalledByGraph proc~kkt_solve sqpopt_kkt_type%kkt_solve proc~direct_qp_step direct_qp_step proc~direct_qp_step->proc~kkt_solve proc~least_squares_min_norm sqpopt_least_squares_type%least_squares_min_norm proc~least_squares_min_norm->proc~kkt_solve proc~least_squares_multipliers sqpopt_least_squares_type%least_squares_multipliers proc~least_squares_multipliers->proc~kkt_solve proc~multiplier_estimate multiplier_estimate proc~multiplier_estimate->proc~least_squares_multipliers proc~restoration_step