Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine eval_jac_cached ( me , x , jac_val ) class ( sqpopt_problem_type ), intent ( inout ) :: me real ( wp ), dimension (:), intent ( in ) :: x !! point `dimension(n)` real ( wp ), dimension (:), intent ( out ) :: jac_val !! scaled Jacobian values `dimension(jac_nnz)` integer :: k call raw_gjac ( me , x , jac_val = jac_val ) do k = 1 , me % jac_nnz jac_val ( k ) = me % c_scale ( me % jac_irow ( k )) * jac_val ( k ) end do end subroutine eval_jac_cached","tags":"","url":"proc/eval_jac_cached.html"},{"title":"raw_fc – sqpopt","text":"private  subroutine raw_fc(me, x, f, c) the unscaled objective and (if c is present) constraints, from the\ncache or the user's fc (whose call is counted, and whose status is\nhandled as by check_status ). The user's function writes straight into\nthe next cache entry, so an evaluation needs no work array. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( sqpopt_problem_type ), intent(inout) :: me real(kind=wp), intent(in), dimension(:) :: x point dimension(n) real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: f objective at x (unscaled) real(kind=wp), intent(out), optional, dimension(:) :: c constraints at x (unscaled) dimension(m) Calls proc~~raw_fc~~CallsGraph proc~raw_fc raw_fc proc~reset_evaluations sqpopt_problem_type%reset_evaluations proc~raw_fc->proc~reset_evaluations proc~wall_time wall_time proc~raw_fc->proc~wall_time Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Called by proc~~raw_fc~~CalledByGraph proc~raw_fc raw_fc proc~eval_c_cached sqpopt_problem_type%eval_c_cached proc~eval_c_cached->proc~raw_fc proc~eval_f_cached sqpopt_problem_type%eval_f_cached proc~eval_f_cached->proc~raw_fc proc~diagnostics_start sqpopt_diagnostics_type%diagnostics_start proc~diagnostics_start->proc~eval_c_cached proc~diagnostics_start->proc~eval_f_cached proc~escape_step escape_step proc~escape_step->proc~eval_c_cached proc~restoration_phase_step sqpopt_restoration_type%restoration_phase_step proc~restoration_phase_step->proc~eval_c_cached proc~restoration_step restoration_step proc~restoration_step->proc~eval_c_cached proc~sqpopt_evaluate_point sqpopt_evaluate_point proc~sqpopt_evaluate_point->proc~eval_c_cached proc~sqpopt_evaluate_point->proc~eval_f_cached proc~sqpopt_iterate sqpopt_iterate proc~sqpopt_iterate->proc~eval_c_cached proc~sqpopt_iterate->proc~eval_f_cached proc~sqpopt_iterate->proc~escape_step proc~sqpopt_iterate->proc~restoration_phase_step proc~sqpopt_iterate->proc~restoration_step proc~trust_region_step sqpopt_trust_region_type%trust_region_step proc~sqpopt_iterate->proc~trust_region_step proc~trust_region_step->proc~eval_c_cached proc~trust_region_step->proc~eval_f_cached proc~sqpopt_solve sqpopt_type%sqpopt_solve proc~sqpopt_solve->proc~diagnostics_start proc~sqpopt_solve->proc~sqpopt_evaluate_point proc~sqpopt_solve->proc~sqpopt_iterate proc~nlls_solve sqpopt_nlls_type%nlls_solve proc~nlls_solve->proc~sqpopt_solve Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine raw_fc ( me , x , f , c ) class ( sqpopt_problem_type ), intent ( inout ) :: me real ( wp ), dimension (:), intent ( in ) :: x !! point `dimension(n)` real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: f !! objective at `x` (unscaled) real ( wp ), dimension (:), optional , intent ( out ) :: c !! constraints at `x` (unscaled) `dimension(m)` real ( wp ) :: t0 !! (for the time spent in the user's function) integer :: k , status if (. not . allocated ( me % cache_x )) call reset_evaluations ( me ) do k = 1 , me % cache_n if ( all ( me % cache_x (:, k ) == x )) then f = me % cache_f ( k ) if ( present ( c )) c = me % cache_c (:, k ) return end if end do if ( me % stop_requested ) then ! (no more user calls once a stop has been requested) f = ieee_value ( 1.0_wp , ieee_quiet_nan ) if ( present ( c )) c = f return end if k = me % cache_next status = 0 t0 = wall_time () if ( associated ( me % user_data )) then call me % eval_fc ( x , me % cache_f ( k ), me % cache_c (:, k ), status , me % user_data ) else call me % eval_fc ( x , me % cache_f ( k ), me % cache_c (:, k ), status ) end if me % time_user = me % time_user + ( wall_time () - t0 ) me % n_eval_fc = me % n_eval_fc + 1 if ( status /= 0 ) then if ( status < 0 ) me % stop_requested = . true . me % cache_f ( k ) = ieee_value ( 1.0_wp , ieee_quiet_nan ) me % cache_c (:, k ) = ieee_value ( 1.0_wp , ieee_quiet_nan ) end if me % cache_x (:, k ) = x me % cache_n = min ( me % cache_n + 1 , cache_size ) me % cache_next = mod ( me % cache_next , cache_size ) + 1 f = me % cache_f ( k ) if ( present ( c )) c = me % cache_c (:, k ) end subroutine raw_fc","tags":"","url":"proc/raw_fc.html"},{"title":"raw_gjac – sqpopt","text":"private  subroutine raw_gjac(me, x, g, jac_val) the unscaled gradient and/or Jacobian values (whichever of g and jac_val is present), from the one-entry cache or the user's gjac (whose call is counted, and whose status is handled as by check_status ). The user's function writes straight into the cache,\nso an evaluation needs no work array. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( sqpopt_problem_type ), intent(inout) :: me real(kind=wp), intent(in), dimension(:) :: x point dimension(n) real(kind=wp), intent(out), optional, dimension(:) :: g objective gradient at x (unscaled) dimension(n) real(kind=wp), intent(out), optional, dimension(:) :: jac_val nonzero Jacobian values at x (unscaled) dimension(jac_nnz) Calls proc~~raw_gjac~~CallsGraph proc~raw_gjac raw_gjac proc~reset_evaluations sqpopt_problem_type%reset_evaluations proc~raw_gjac->proc~reset_evaluations proc~wall_time wall_time proc~raw_gjac->proc~wall_time Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Called by proc~~raw_gjac~~CalledByGraph proc~raw_gjac raw_gjac proc~compute_scaling sqpopt_problem_type%compute_scaling proc~compute_scaling->proc~raw_gjac proc~eval_g_cached sqpopt_problem_type%eval_g_cached proc~eval_g_cached->proc~raw_gjac proc~eval_jac_cached sqpopt_problem_type%eval_jac_cached proc~eval_jac_cached->proc~raw_gjac proc~diagnostics_start sqpopt_diagnostics_type%diagnostics_start proc~diagnostics_start->proc~eval_jac_cached proc~sqpopt_evaluate_point sqpopt_evaluate_point proc~sqpopt_evaluate_point->proc~eval_jac_cached proc~sqpopt_iterate sqpopt_iterate proc~sqpopt_iterate->proc~eval_jac_cached proc~sqpopt_solve sqpopt_type%sqpopt_solve proc~sqpopt_solve->proc~compute_scaling proc~sqpopt_solve->proc~diagnostics_start proc~sqpopt_solve->proc~sqpopt_evaluate_point proc~sqpopt_solve->proc~sqpopt_iterate proc~nlls_solve sqpopt_nlls_type%nlls_solve proc~nlls_solve->proc~sqpopt_solve Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine raw_gjac ( me , x , g , jac_val ) class ( sqpopt_problem_type ), intent ( inout ) :: me real ( wp ), dimension (:), intent ( in ) :: x !! point `dimension(n)` real ( wp ), dimension (:), optional , intent ( out ) :: g !! objective gradient at `x` (unscaled) `dimension(n)` real ( wp ), dimension (:), optional , intent ( out ) :: jac_val !! nonzero Jacobian values at `x` (unscaled) !! `dimension(jac_nnz)` real ( wp ) :: t0 !! (for the time spent in the user's function) integer :: status logical :: cached if (. not . allocated ( me % cache_xg )) call reset_evaluations ( me ) cached = . false . if ( me % have_gjac ) cached = all ( me % cache_xg == x ) if (. not . cached ) then if ( me % stop_requested ) then ! (no more user calls once a stop has been requested) if ( present ( g )) g = ieee_value ( 1.0_wp , ieee_quiet_nan ) if ( present ( jac_val )) jac_val = ieee_value ( 1.0_wp , ieee_quiet_nan ) return end if me % have_gjac = . false . status = 0 t0 = wall_time () if ( associated ( me % user_data )) then call me % eval_gjac ( x , me % cache_g , me % cache_jac , me % derivative_accuracy , status , me % user_data ) else call me % eval_gjac ( x , me % cache_g , me % cache_jac , me % derivative_accuracy , status ) end if me % time_user = me % time_user + ( wall_time () - t0 ) me % n_eval_gjac = me % n_eval_gjac + 1 if ( status /= 0 ) then if ( status < 0 ) me % stop_requested = . true . me % cache_g = ieee_value ( 1.0_wp , ieee_quiet_nan ) me % cache_jac = ieee_value ( 1.0_wp , ieee_quiet_nan ) end if me % cache_xg = x me % have_gjac = . true . end if if ( present ( g )) g = me % cache_g if ( present ( jac_val )) jac_val = me % cache_jac end subroutine raw_gjac","tags":"","url":"proc/raw_gjac.html"},{"title":"eval_hess_scaled – sqpopt","text":"private  subroutine eval_hess_scaled(me, x, lambda, hess_val) the nonzero values of the Hessian of the (scaled) Lagrangian at x , for\nthe multipliers lambda of the scaled problem: the user's hess is\ncalled with the multipliers of the original problem, , and its values are multiplied by .\nNaN if the user function failed ( status /= 0 ). Type Bound sqpopt_problem_type Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( sqpopt_problem_type ), intent(inout) :: me real(kind=wp), intent(in), dimension(:) :: x point dimension(n) real(kind=wp), intent(in), dimension(:) :: lambda multipliers of the scaled problem dimension(m) real(kind=wp), intent(out), dimension(:) :: hess_val scaled Hessian values dimension(hess_nnz) Calls proc~~eval_hess_scaled~~CallsGraph proc~eval_hess_scaled sqpopt_problem_type%eval_hess_scaled proc~check_status check_status proc~eval_hess_scaled->proc~check_status proc~wall_time wall_time proc~eval_hess_scaled->proc~wall_time Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Called by proc~~eval_hess_scaled~~CalledByGraph proc~eval_hess_scaled sqpopt_problem_type%eval_hess_scaled proc~sqpopt_iterate sqpopt_iterate proc~sqpopt_iterate->proc~eval_hess_scaled proc~sqpopt_solve sqpopt_type%sqpopt_solve proc~sqpopt_solve->proc~sqpopt_iterate proc~nlls_solve sqpopt_nlls_type%nlls_solve proc~nlls_solve->proc~sqpopt_solve Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine eval_hess_scaled ( me , x , lambda , hess_val ) class ( sqpopt_problem_type ), intent ( inout ) :: me real ( wp ), dimension (:), intent ( in ) :: x !! point `dimension(n)` real ( wp ), dimension (:), intent ( in ) :: lambda !! multipliers of the scaled problem `dimension(m)` real ( wp ), dimension (:), intent ( out ) :: hess_val !! scaled Hessian values `dimension(hess_nnz)` real ( wp ) :: t0 !! (for the time spent in the user's function) integer :: status real ( wp ), dimension (:), allocatable :: lambda_user !! the multipliers of the original problem if ( me % stop_requested . or . . not . associated ( me % eval_hess )) then hess_val = ieee_value ( 1.0_wp , ieee_quiet_nan ) return end if allocate ( lambda_user ( size ( lambda ))) lambda_user = lambda * me % c_scale / me % f_scale status = 0 t0 = wall_time () if ( associated ( me % user_data )) then call me % eval_hess ( x , lambda_user , hess_val , status , me % user_data ) else call me % eval_hess ( x , lambda_user , hess_val , status ) end if me % time_user = me % time_user + ( wall_time () - t0 ) me % n_eval_hess = me % n_eval_hess + 1 call check_status ( me , status , hess_val ) hess_val = me % f_scale * hess_val end subroutine eval_hess_scaled","tags":"","url":"proc/eval_hess_scaled.html"},{"title":"check_status – sqpopt","text":"private  subroutine check_status(me, status, v) handle a user function's returned status : if it is nonzero the\noutputs v are replaced by NaN (so the solver rejects the point, or\nreports sqpopt_function_error if it is the current point), and if it\nis negative a stop is requested (after which no user function is called\nagain: uncached evaluations just return NaN). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( sqpopt_problem_type ), intent(inout) :: me integer, intent(in) :: status the status the user function returned real(kind=wp), intent(inout), dimension(:) :: v the values it returned (set to NaN if it could not evaluate them) Called by proc~~check_status~~CalledByGraph proc~check_status check_status proc~eval_hess_scaled sqpopt_problem_type%eval_hess_scaled proc~eval_hess_scaled->proc~check_status proc~sqpopt_iterate sqpopt_iterate proc~sqpopt_iterate->proc~eval_hess_scaled proc~sqpopt_solve sqpopt_type%sqpopt_solve proc~sqpopt_solve->proc~sqpopt_iterate proc~nlls_solve sqpopt_nlls_type%nlls_solve proc~nlls_solve->proc~sqpopt_solve Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine check_status ( me , status , v ) class ( sqpopt_problem_type ), intent ( inout ) :: me integer , intent ( in ) :: status !! the `status` the user function returned real ( wp ), dimension (:), intent ( inout ) :: v !! the values it returned (set to NaN if it could not evaluate them) if ( status == 0 ) return if ( status < 0 ) me % stop_requested = . true . v = ieee_value ( 1.0_wp , ieee_quiet_nan ) end subroutine check_status","tags":"","url":"proc/check_status.html"},{"title":"set_derivative_accuracy – sqpopt","text":"private  subroutine set_derivative_accuracy(me, accuracy) set the accuracy the user's gjac is asked for ( sqpopt_derivatives_fast or sqpopt_derivatives_accurate ). A change empties the gjac cache, so\nthat derivatives at a point already evaluated are evaluated again, at the\nnew accuracy. Type Bound sqpopt_problem_type Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( sqpopt_problem_type ), intent(inout) :: me integer, intent(in) :: accuracy sqpopt_derivatives_fast or sqpopt_derivatives_accurate Called by proc~~set_derivative_accuracy~~CalledByGraph proc~set_derivative_accuracy sqpopt_problem_type%set_derivative_accuracy proc~sqpopt_iterate sqpopt_iterate proc~sqpopt_iterate->proc~set_derivative_accuracy proc~sqpopt_solve sqpopt_type%sqpopt_solve proc~sqpopt_solve->proc~set_derivative_accuracy proc~sqpopt_solve->proc~sqpopt_iterate proc~nlls_solve sqpopt_nlls_type%nlls_solve proc~nlls_solve->proc~sqpopt_solve Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to p