vector `dimension(n)` real ( wp ), dimension (:), intent ( in ) :: y !! Lagrangian gradient change `dimension(n)` real ( wp ), dimension (:), allocatable :: bs , w real ( wp ) :: denom , sty , yty if ( me % exact ) return ! a near-zero step carries no reliable curvature information and risks ! an ill-conditioned update, so skip it outright: if ( norm2 ( s ) <= 1.0e-10_wp ) return allocate ( bs ( me % n ), w ( me % n )) call hessian_vector_product ( me , s , bs ) w = y - bs denom = dot_product ( w , s ) ! standard SR1 safeguard against a near-singular update: if ( abs ( denom ) < 1.0e-8_wp * max ( norm2 ( w ) * norm2 ( s ), 1.0e-12_wp )) return call hessian_push_pair ( me , s , y ) sty = dot_product ( s , y ) yty = dot_product ( y , y ) if ( sty > 0.0_wp . and . yty > 0.0_wp ) me % gamma = sty / yty end subroutine hessian_update_sr1","tags":"","url":"proc/hessian_update_sr1.html"},{"title":"hessian_push_pair – sqpopt","text":"private  subroutine hessian_push_pair(me, s, y) push a new (s,y) pair into the circular history buffer, discarding\nthe oldest pair if max_history pairs are already stored (by\noverwriting its column and advancing first , so no data is moved), and\nupdate the inner products ss and sy with the new pair ( O(nk) ). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( sqpopt_hessian_type ), intent(inout) :: me real(kind=wp), intent(in), dimension(:) :: s step vector dimension(n) real(kind=wp), intent(in), dimension(:) :: y Lagrangian gradient change dimension(n) Calls proc~~hessian_push_pair~~CallsGraph proc~hessian_push_pair hessian_push_pair proc~pair_col pair_col proc~hessian_push_pair->proc~pair_col Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Called by proc~~hessian_push_pair~~CalledByGraph proc~hessian_push_pair hessian_push_pair proc~hessian_update_bfgs sqpopt_hessian_type%hessian_update_bfgs proc~hessian_update_bfgs->proc~hessian_push_pair proc~hessian_update_sr1 sqpopt_hessian_type%hessian_update_sr1 proc~hessian_update_sr1->proc~hessian_push_pair proc~sqpopt_iterate sqpopt_iterate proc~sqpopt_iterate->proc~hessian_update_bfgs proc~sqpopt_iterate->proc~hessian_update_sr1 proc~sqpopt_solve sqpopt_type%sqpopt_solve proc~sqpopt_solve->proc~sqpopt_iterate proc~nlls_solve sqpopt_nlls_type%nlls_solve proc~nlls_solve->proc~sqpopt_solve Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine hessian_push_pair ( me , s , y ) class ( sqpopt_hessian_type ), intent ( inout ) :: me real ( wp ), dimension (:), intent ( in ) :: s !! step vector `dimension(n)` real ( wp ), dimension (:), intent ( in ) :: y !! Lagrangian gradient change `dimension(n)` integer :: i , j , c if ( me % n_history == me % max_history ) then me % first = mod ( me % first , me % max_history ) + 1 ! the oldest pair's column becomes the newest else me % n_history = me % n_history + 1 end if c = pair_col ( me , me % n_history ) me % s (:, c ) = s me % y (:, c ) = y do i = 1 , me % n_history j = pair_col ( me , i ) me % ss ( c , j ) = dot_product ( s , me % s (:, j )) me % ss ( j , c ) = me % ss ( c , j ) me % sy ( c , j ) = dot_product ( s , me % y (:, j )) me % sy ( j , c ) = dot_product ( me % s (:, j ), y ) end do me % mid_valid = . false . end subroutine hessian_push_pair","tags":"","url":"proc/hessian_push_pair.html"},{"title":"hessian_vector_product – sqpopt","text":"private  subroutine hessian_vector_product(me, v, hv) compute the matrix-free Hessian-vector product , used\nby the QP subproblem solver in place of an explicit dense matrix.\nUses the compact representation of either the BFGS or the SR1\nmatrix (Byrd, Nocedal & Schnabel, 1994), depending on use_sr1 , with\nits small middle matrix factored once (see factor_middle_matrix )\nand reused until the pairs or gamma change. Type Bound sqpopt_hessian_type Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( sqpopt_hessian_type ), intent(inout) :: me real(kind=wp), intent(in), dimension(:) :: v input vector dimension(n) real(kind=wp), intent(out), dimension(:) :: hv result dimension(n) Calls proc~~hessian_vector_product~~CallsGraph proc~hessian_vector_product sqpopt_hessian_type%hessian_vector_product proc~dense_lu_solve dense_lu_solve proc~hessian_vector_product->proc~dense_lu_solve proc~factor_middle_matrix factor_middle_matrix proc~hessian_vector_product->proc~factor_middle_matrix proc~pair_col pair_col proc~hessian_vector_product->proc~pair_col proc~dense_lu_factor dense_lu_factor proc~factor_middle_matrix->proc~dense_lu_factor proc~middle_matrix middle_matrix proc~factor_middle_matrix->proc~middle_matrix proc~middle_matrix->proc~pair_col Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Called by proc~~hessian_vector_product~~CalledByGraph proc~hessian_vector_product sqpopt_hessian_type%hessian_vector_product proc~direct_qp_step direct_qp_step proc~direct_qp_step->proc~hessian_vector_product proc~hessian_cg_solve hessian_cg_solve proc~hessian_cg_solve->proc~hessian_vector_product proc~hessian_dense sqpopt_hessian_type%hessian_dense proc~hessian_dense->proc~hessian_vector_product proc~hessian_update_bfgs sqpopt_hessian_type%hessian_update_bfgs proc~hessian_update_bfgs->proc~hessian_vector_product proc~hessian_update_sr1 sqpopt_hessian_type%hessian_update_sr1 proc~hessian_update_sr1->proc~hessian_vector_product proc~solve_reduced_hessian_qp sqpopt_reduced_hessian_qp_type%solve_reduced_hessian_qp proc~solve_reduced_hessian_qp->proc~hessian_vector_product proc~sqpopt_iterate sqpopt_iterate proc~sqpopt_iterate->proc~hessian_vector_product proc~sqpopt_iterate->proc~hessian_update_bfgs proc~sqpopt_iterate->proc~hessian_update_sr1 proc~trust_region_step sqpopt_trust_region_type%trust_region_step proc~sqpopt_iterate->proc~trust_region_step proc~solve_qp_subproblem sqpopt_qp_solver_type%solve_qp_subproblem proc~sqpopt_iterate->proc~solve_qp_subproblem proc~restoration_phase_step sqpopt_restoration_type%restoration_phase_step proc~sqpopt_iterate->proc~restoration_phase_step proc~trust_region_step->proc~hessian_vector_product proc~trust_region_step->proc~solve_qp_subproblem proc~hessian_inverse_vector_product sqpopt_hessian_type%hessian_inverse_vector_product proc~hessian_inverse_vector_product->proc~hessian_cg_solve proc~solve_dense_qp sqpopt_dense_qp_type%solve_dense_qp proc~solve_dense_qp->proc~hessian_dense proc~solve_qp_subproblem->proc~direct_qp_step proc~solve_qp_subproblem->proc~hessian_inverse_vector_product proc~solve_qp_subproblem->proc~solve_dense_qp proc~sqpopt_solve sqpopt_type%sqpopt_solve proc~sqpopt_solve->proc~sqpopt_iterate proc~nlls_solve sqpopt_nlls_type%nlls_solve proc~nlls_solve->proc~sqpopt_solve proc~restoration_phase_step->proc~solve_qp_subproblem Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine hessian_vector_product ( me , v , hv ) class ( sqpopt_hessian_type ), intent ( inout ) :: me real ( wp ), dimension (:), intent ( in ) :: v !! input vector `dimension(n)` real ( wp ), dimension (:), intent ( out ) :: hv !! result `dimension(n)` integer :: i , k , c real ( wp ), dimension (:), allocatable :: w real ( wp ) :: theta if ( me % exact ) then ! H*v from the nonzeros (each off-diagonal one stands for both ! (i,j) and (j,i)), plus the shift: hv = me % shift * v do k = 1 , size ( me % h_val ) i = me % h_irow ( k ) c = me % h_icol ( k ) hv ( i ) = hv ( i ) + me % h_val ( k ) * v ( c ) if ( i /= c ) hv ( c ) = hv ( c ) + me % h_val ( k ) * v ( i ) end do return end if k = me % n_history theta = 1.0_wp / me % gamma hv = ( theta + me % shift ) * v if ( k == 0 ) return if (. not . me % mid_valid ) call factor_middle_matrix ( me ) if (. not . me % mid_ok ) return ! singular middle matrix: fall back to the (safe) initial scaling if ( me % use_sr1 ) then ! B*v = theta*v + Psi * M&#94;{-1} * Psi&#94;T v, with Psi = Y - theta*S allocate ( w ( k )) do i = 1 , k c = pair_col ( me , i ) w ( i ) = dot_product ( me % y (:, c ), v ) - theta * dot_product ( me % s (:, c ), v ) end do call lu_solve ( me % mid_lu , me % mid_piv , w ) do i = 1 , k c = pair_col ( me , i ) hv = hv + ( me % y (:, c ) - theta * me % s (:, c )) * w ( i ) end do else ! B*v = theta*v - [theta*S Y] * M&#94;{-1} * [theta*S&#94;T v; Y&#94;T v] allocate ( w ( 2 * k )) do i = 1 , k c = pair_col ( me , i ) w ( i ) = theta * dot_product ( me % s (:, c ), v ) w ( k + i ) = dot_product ( me % y (:, c ), v ) end do call lu_solve ( me % mid_lu , me % mid_piv , w ) do i = 1 , k c = pair_col ( me , i ) hv = hv - theta * me % s (:, c ) * w ( i ) - me % y (:, c ) * w ( k + i ) end do end if end subroutine hessian_vector_product","tags":"","url":"proc/hessian_vector_product.html"},{"title":"hessian_diagonal – sqpopt","text":"private  subroutine hessian_diagonal(me, d) the diagonal of the Hessian approximation , from its compact\nrepresentation (at a cost of for k pairs, without\nforming ): , with the i -th row of (BFGS, minus)\nor of (SR1, plus), i.e. the row sums of . Used as a (Jacobi) preconditioner. The\nresult is kept until the pairs or the scaling change. Type Bound sqpopt_hessian_type Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( sqpopt_hessian_type ), intent(inout) :: me real(kind=wp), intent(out), dimension(:) :: d the diagonal dimension(n) Calls proc~~hessian_diagonal~~CallsGraph proc~hessian_diagonal sqpopt_hessian_type%hessian_diagonal proc~dense_lu_solve dense_lu_solve proc~hessian_diagonal->proc~dense_lu_solve proc~factor_middle_matrix factor_middle_matrix proc~hessian_diagonal->proc~factor_middle_matrix proc~pair_col pair_col proc~hessian_diagonal->proc~pair_col proc~dense_lu_factor dense_lu_factor proc~factor_middle_matrix->proc~dense_lu_factor proc~middle_matrix middle_matrix proc~factor_middle_matrix->proc~middle_matrix proc~middle_matrix->proc~pair_col Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Called by proc~~hessian_diagonal~~CalledByGraph proc~hessian_diagonal sqpopt_hessian_type%hessian_diagonal proc~solve_reduced_hessian_qp sqpopt_reduced_hessian_qp_type%solve_reduced_hessian_qp proc~solve_reduced_hessian_qp->proc~hessian_diagonal Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine hessian_diagonal ( me , d ) class ( sqpopt_hessian_type ), intent ( inout ) :: me real ( wp ), dimension (:), intent ( out ) :: d !! the diagonal `dimension(n)` integer :: i , k , c , nk , j real ( wp ) :: theta real ( wp ), dimension (:,:), allocatable :: psi , minv , pm if ( me % exact ) then d = me % shift do k = 1 , size ( me % h_val ) if ( me % h_irow ( k ) == me % h_icol ( k )) d ( me % h_irow ( k )) = d ( me % h_irow ( k )) + me % h_val ( k ) end do return end if k = me % n_history theta = 1.0_wp / me % gamma d = theta + me % shift if ( k == 0 ) return if (. not . me % mid_valid ) call factor_middle_matrix ( me ) if (. not . me % mid_ok ) return if ( me % diag_valid ) then d = me % diag + me % shift return end if nk = merge ( k , 2 * k , me % use_sr1 ) allocate ( psi ( me % n , nk ), minv ( nk , nk )) do i = 1 , k c = pair_col ( me , i ) if ( me % use_sr1 ) then psi (:, i ) = me % y (:, c ) - theta * me % s (:, c ) else psi (:, i ) = theta * me % s (:, c ) psi (:, k + i ) = me % y (:, c ) end if end do minv = 0.0_wp do j = 1 , nk minv ( j , j ) = 1.0_wp call lu_solve ( me % mid_lu , me % mid_piv , minv (:, j )) end do pm = matmul ( psi , minv ) me % diag = theta + merge ( 1.0_wp , - 1.0_wp , me % use_sr1 ) * sum ( psi * pm , dim = 2 ) me % diag_valid = . true . d = me % diag + me % shift end subroutine hessian_diagonal","tags":"","url":"proc/hessian_diagonal.html"},{"title":"hessian_dense – sqpopt","text":"private  subroutine hessian_dense(me, h) the Hessian approximation as a dense matrix, in the caller's\narray (for the dense QP solver, the only place a dense matrix is used). For BFGS, is built by applying the stored updates, oldest\nfirst, to : which is the matrix of the compact representation that hessian_vector_product uses (Byrd, Nocedal & Schnabel, 1994), at multiplications per pair (only the upper triangle is\nupdated). Forming it from n products instead costs about each, i.e. per pair, which is 4 times\nas much with k = n pairs. A pair is skipped if isn't\npositive, which can only happen through round-off: every stored pair has , so each update keeps positive definite. Where hessian_vector_product falls back to (it takes the\nmiddle matrix to be singular), so does this, so that the QP's matrix is\nthe one the products elsewhere in the iteration are made with. For SR1 (whose updates needn't all be defined one at a time) is\nformed from the products with the unit vectors (and symmetrized), and\nin exact mode from the nonzeros and the shift. Type Bound sqpopt_hessian_type Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( sqpopt_hessian_type ), intent(inout) :: me real(kind=wp), intent(out), dimension(:,:) :: h the matrix dimension(n,n) (symmetric, both triangles set) Calls proc~~hessian_dense~~CallsGraph proc~hessian_dense sqpopt_hessian_type%hessian_dense proc~factor_middle_