gate-gradient solve driven by hessian_vector_product . Type Bound sqpopt_hessian_type Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( sqpopt_hessian_type ), intent(inout) :: me real(kind=wp), intent(in), dimension(:) :: v input vector dimension(n) real(kind=wp), intent(out), dimension(:) :: d result dimension(n) Calls proc~~hessian_inverse_vector_product~~CallsGraph proc~hessian_inverse_vector_product sqpopt_hessian_type%hessian_inverse_vector_product proc~hessian_cg_solve hessian_cg_solve proc~hessian_inverse_vector_product->proc~hessian_cg_solve proc~pair_col pair_col proc~hessian_inverse_vector_product->proc~pair_col proc~hessian_vector_product sqpopt_hessian_type%hessian_vector_product proc~hessian_cg_solve->proc~hessian_vector_product proc~hessian_vector_product->proc~pair_col proc~dense_lu_solve dense_lu_solve proc~hessian_vector_product->proc~dense_lu_solve proc~factor_middle_matrix factor_middle_matrix proc~hessian_vector_product->proc~factor_middle_matrix proc~dense_lu_factor dense_lu_factor proc~factor_middle_matrix->proc~dense_lu_factor proc~middle_matrix middle_matrix proc~factor_middle_matrix->proc~middle_matrix proc~middle_matrix->proc~pair_col Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Called by proc~~hessian_inverse_vector_product~~CalledByGraph proc~hessian_inverse_vector_product sqpopt_hessian_type%hessian_inverse_vector_product proc~solve_qp_subproblem sqpopt_qp_solver_type%solve_qp_subproblem proc~solve_qp_subproblem->proc~hessian_inverse_vector_product proc~restoration_phase_step sqpopt_restoration_type%restoration_phase_step proc~restoration_phase_step->proc~solve_qp_subproblem proc~sqpopt_iterate sqpopt_iterate proc~sqpopt_iterate->proc~solve_qp_subproblem proc~sqpopt_iterate->proc~restoration_phase_step proc~trust_region_step sqpopt_trust_region_type%trust_region_step proc~sqpopt_iterate->proc~trust_region_step proc~trust_region_step->proc~solve_qp_subproblem proc~sqpopt_solve sqpopt_type%sqpopt_solve proc~sqpopt_solve->proc~sqpopt_iterate proc~nlls_solve sqpopt_nlls_type%nlls_solve proc~nlls_solve->proc~sqpopt_solve Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine hessian_inverse_vector_product ( me , v , d ) class ( sqpopt_hessian_type ), intent ( inout ) :: me real ( wp ), dimension (:), intent ( in ) :: v !! input vector `dimension(n)` real ( wp ), dimension (:), intent ( out ) :: d !! result `dimension(n)` real ( wp ), dimension (:), allocatable :: alpha !! temporary storage for the two-loop recursion coefficients in L-BFGS real ( wp ), dimension (:), allocatable :: q !! temporary vector used in the two-loop recursion integer :: i !! loop index for the two-loop recursion integer :: c !! column of the `i`-th pair real ( wp ) :: beta if ( me % use_sr1 . or . me % exact ) then call hessian_cg_solve ( me , v , d ) return end if ! standard L-BFGS two-loop recursion: allocate ( alpha ( me % n_history ), q ( me % n )) q = v do i = me % n_history , 1 , - 1 c = pair_col ( me , i ) alpha ( i ) = me % rho ( c ) * dot_product ( me % s (:, c ), q ) q = q - alpha ( i ) * me % y (:, c ) end do d = me % gamma * q do i = 1 , me % n_history c = pair_col ( me , i ) beta = me % rho ( c ) * dot_product ( me % y (:, c ), d ) d = d + me % s (:, c ) * ( alpha ( i ) - beta ) end do end subroutine hessian_inverse_vector_product","tags":"","url":"proc/hessian_inverse_vector_product.html"},{"title":"hessian_cg_solve – sqpopt","text":"private  subroutine hessian_cg_solve(me, v, d) approximate via a small conjugate-gradient solve of , using only hessian_vector_product (matrix-free).\n Used for the SR1 mode, which has no simple closed-form inverse. indefinite/singular direction: stop and return current estimate Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( sqpopt_hessian_type ), intent(inout) :: me real(kind=wp), intent(in), dimension(:) :: v right-hand side dimension(n) real(kind=wp), intent(out), dimension(:) :: d solution of dimension(n) Calls proc~~hessian_cg_solve~~CallsGraph proc~hessian_cg_solve hessian_cg_solve proc~hessian_vector_product sqpopt_hessian_type%hessian_vector_product proc~hessian_cg_solve->proc~hessian_vector_product proc~dense_lu_solve dense_lu_solve proc~hessian_vector_product->proc~dense_lu_solve proc~factor_middle_matrix factor_middle_matrix proc~hessian_vector_product->proc~factor_middle_matrix proc~pair_col pair_col proc~hessian_vector_product->proc~pair_col proc~dense_lu_factor dense_lu_factor proc~factor_middle_matrix->proc~dense_lu_factor proc~middle_matrix middle_matrix proc~factor_middle_matrix->proc~middle_matrix proc~middle_matrix->proc~pair_col Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Called by proc~~hessian_cg_solve~~CalledByGraph proc~hessian_cg_solve hessian_cg_solve proc~hessian_inverse_vector_product sqpopt_hessian_type%hessian_inverse_vector_product proc~hessian_inverse_vector_product->proc~hessian_cg_solve proc~solve_qp_subproblem sqpopt_qp_solver_type%solve_qp_subproblem proc~solve_qp_subproblem->proc~hessian_inverse_vector_product proc~restoration_phase_step sqpopt_restoration_type%restoration_phase_step proc~restoration_phase_step->proc~solve_qp_subproblem proc~sqpopt_iterate sqpopt_iterate proc~sqpopt_iterate->proc~solve_qp_subproblem proc~sqpopt_iterate->proc~restoration_phase_step proc~trust_region_step sqpopt_trust_region_type%trust_region_step proc~sqpopt_iterate->proc~trust_region_step proc~trust_region_step->proc~solve_qp_subproblem proc~sqpopt_solve sqpopt_type%sqpopt_solve proc~sqpopt_solve->proc~sqpopt_iterate proc~nlls_solve sqpopt_nlls_type%nlls_solve proc~nlls_solve->proc~sqpopt_solve Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine hessian_cg_solve ( me , v , d ) class ( sqpopt_hessian_type ), intent ( inout ) :: me real ( wp ), dimension (:), intent ( in ) :: v !! right-hand side `dimension(n)` real ( wp ), dimension (:), intent ( out ) :: d !! solution of  B d = v  `dimension(n)` real ( wp ), dimension (:), allocatable :: r , p , hp real ( wp ) :: rs_old , rs_new , alpha , beta , pHp integer :: iter , maxit allocate ( r ( me % n ), p ( me % n ), hp ( me % n )) d = 0.0_wp r = v p = r rs_old = dot_product ( r , r ) if ( rs_old <= 0.0_wp ) return maxit = min ( me % n , max ( 2 * me % max_history , 10 )) do iter = 1 , maxit call hessian_vector_product ( me , p , hp ) pHp = dot_product ( p , hp ) if ( abs ( pHp ) < 1.0e-14_wp ) exit !! indefinite/singular direction: stop and return current estimate alpha = rs_old / pHp d = d + alpha * p r = r - alpha * hp rs_new = dot_product ( r , r ) if ( sqrt ( rs_new ) <= 1.0e-10_wp * max ( norm2 ( v ), 1.0_wp )) exit beta = rs_new / rs_old p = r + beta * p rs_old = rs_new end do end subroutine hessian_cg_solve","tags":"","url":"proc/hessian_cg_solve.html"},{"title":"hessian_reset – sqpopt","text":"private  subroutine hessian_reset(me) reset the Hessian approximation, discarding all stored (s,y) pairs\n(and any shift). In exact mode, increase the shift instead (see the\nmodule documentation). Type Bound sqpopt_hessian_type Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( sqpopt_hessian_type ), intent(inout) :: me Calls proc~~hessian_reset~~CallsGraph proc~hessian_reset sqpopt_hessian_type%hessian_reset proc~hessian_size sqpopt_hessian_type%hessian_size proc~hessian_reset->proc~hessian_size Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Called by proc~~hessian_reset~~CalledByGraph proc~hessian_reset sqpopt_hessian_type%hessian_reset proc~sqpopt_iterate sqpopt_iterate proc~sqpopt_iterate->proc~hessian_reset proc~sqpopt_solve sqpopt_type%sqpopt_solve proc~sqpopt_solve->proc~sqpopt_iterate proc~nlls_solve sqpopt_nlls_type%nlls_solve proc~nlls_solve->proc~sqpopt_solve Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine hessian_reset ( me ) class ( sqpopt_hessian_type ), intent ( inout ) :: me if ( me % exact ) then ! increase the shift (primal inertia correction, see the module documentation): me % shift = min ( max ( me % shift_min * hessian_size ( me ), 1 0.0_wp * me % shift ), me % shift_max * hessian_size ( me )) return end if me % n_history = 0 me % first = 1 me % gamma = me % gamma0 me % mid_valid = . false . me % shift = 0.0_wp end subroutine hessian_reset","tags":"","url":"proc/hessian_reset.html"},{"title":"hessian_set_exact – sqpopt","text":"private  subroutine hessian_set_exact(me, irow, icol) switch to the exact mode (see the module documentation), with the\nsparsity pattern irow / icol of the Hessian of the Lagrangian (each\noff-diagonal element given once, see set_hessian_sparsity ). The\nvalues are set by hessian_set_values ; until then they are zero. Type Bound sqpopt_hessian_type Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( sqpopt_hessian_type ), intent(inout) :: me integer, intent(in), dimension(:) :: irow row indices dimension(nnz) integer, intent(in), dimension(:) :: icol column indices dimension(nnz) Called by proc~~hessian_set_exact~~CalledByGraph proc~hessian_set_exact sqpopt_hessian_type%hessian_set_exact proc~sqpopt_solve sqpopt_type%sqpopt_solve proc~sqpopt_solve->proc~hessian_set_exact proc~nlls_solve sqpopt_nlls_type%nlls_solve proc~nlls_solve->proc~sqpopt_solve Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine hessian_set_exact ( me , irow , icol ) class ( sqpopt_hessian_type ), intent ( inout ) :: me integer , dimension (:), intent ( in ) :: irow !! row indices `dimension(nnz)` integer , dimension (:), intent ( in ) :: icol !! column indices `dimension(nnz)` me % exact = . true . me % h_irow = irow me % h_icol = icol if ( allocated ( me % h_val )) deallocate ( me % h_val ) allocate ( me % h_val ( size ( irow ))) me % h_val = 0.0_wp me % shift = 0.0_wp end subroutine hessian_set_exact","tags":"","url":"proc/hessian_set_exact.html"},{"title":"hessian_set_values – sqpopt","text":"private  subroutine hessian_set_values(me, val, decay) set the values of the exact Hessian for a new major iteration, and, if decay , decrease the shift (divided by 3, and set to 0 once below its\nminimum). Type Bound sqpopt_hessian_type Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( sqpopt_hessian_type ), intent(inout) :: me real(kind=wp), intent(in), dimension(:) :: val the nonzero values dimension(nnz) logical, intent(in) :: decay whether to decrease the shift (after a good step) Calls proc~~hessian_set_values~~CallsGraph proc~hessian_set_values sqpopt_hessian_type%hessian_set_values proc~hessian_size sqpopt_hessian_type%hessian_size proc~hessian_set_values->proc~hessian_size Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Called by proc~~hessian_set_values~~CalledByGraph proc~hessian_set_values sqpopt_hessian_type%hessian_set_values proc~sqpopt_iterate sqpopt_iterate proc~sqpopt_iterate->proc~hessian_set_values proc~sqpopt_solve sqpopt_type%sqpopt_solve proc~sqpopt_solve->proc~sqpopt_iterate proc~nlls_solve sqpopt_nlls_type%nlls_solve proc~nlls_solve->proc~sqpopt_solve Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine hessian_set_values ( me , val , decay ) class ( sqpopt_hessian_type ), intent ( inout ) :: me real ( wp ), dimension (:), intent ( in ) :: val !! the nonzero values `dimension(nnz)` logical , intent ( in ) :: decay !! whether to decrease the shift (after a good step) me % h_val = val if ( decay ) me % shift = me % shift / 3.0_wp if ( me % shift < me % shift_min * hessian_size ( me )) me % shift = 0.0_wp end subroutine hessian_set_values","tags":"","url":"proc/hessian_set_values.html"},{"title":"sqpopt_module – sqpopt","text":"Module containing the main object-oriented interface to the sqpopt Sequential Quadratic Programming solver. It is used via the sqpopt_type class, which is the only public entity in this module.\nThe other components of the algorithm (problem definition, options,\nHessian approximation, QP subproblem solvers, line search, merit\nfunction, filter and funnel, trust region, feasibility restoration,\nsecond-order correction, convergence checking, the optional sparse\nfactorizations (inertia control, direct QP steps, and direct\nleast-squares solves), the diagnostics, and the detailed log)\nare each implemented in their own module so that they may be\ndeveloped, tested, and swapped out independently. Internally, sparse\n(COO) storage is used for the constraint Jacobian, and the Hessian of\nthe Lagrangian is a matrix-free limited-memory operator (or the user's\nsparse exact Hessian), so dense n x n / m x n arrays are only formed\nby the dense QP solver (used for small problems, see sqpopt_qp_solver_module ). Uses sqpopt_problem_module sqpopt_qp_reduced_hessian_module sqpopt_linesearch_module sqpopt_restoration_module sqpopt_hessian_module sqpopt_diagnostics_module sqpopt_qp_solver_module sqpopt_iterate_module sqpopt_types_module sqpopt_options_module sqpopt_trust_region_module sqpopt_log_module sqpopt_inertia_module sqpopt_kkt_module sqpopt_symmetric_solver_module iso_fortran_env sqpopt_kinds sqpopt_least_squares_module module~~sqpopt_module~~UsesGraph module~sqpopt_module sqpopt_module iso_fortran_env iso_fortran_env module~sqpopt_module->iso_fortran_env module~sqpopt_diagnostics_module sqpopt_diagnostics_module module~sqpopt_module->module~sqpopt_diagnostics_module module~sqpopt_hessian_module sqpopt_hessian_module module~sqpopt_module->module~sqpopt_hessian_module module~sqpopt_inertia_module sqpopt_inertia_module module~sqpopt_module