s changes along the steps\ndisagreed with its gradient (see derivative_suspects ) integer, public, dimension(:), allocatable :: derivative_suspects the constraints whose changes along the steps\ndisagreed with their Jacobian rows in most of\nthe steps (the worst first, at most 5): their\nderivatives may be wrong integer, public :: slowest_iteration = 0 the iteration that took the most time real(kind=wp), public :: slowest_iteration_time = 0.0_wp its time (seconds) real(kind=wp), public :: constraint_gradient_ratio = 0.0_wp the largest over the smallest size of a constraint's\ngradient at the starting point ( 0 : no constraints) real(kind=wp), public :: variable_gradient_ratio = 0.0_wp the largest over the smallest size of a variable's\ncolumn of the objective gradient and the Jacobian there integer, public :: n_constant_constraints = 0 constraints with no entry in the Jacobian's pattern integer, public :: n_single_variable_constraints = 0 constraints with a single entry there (a bound on the\nvariable, if they are linear) integer, public :: n_dependent_equalities = -1 equality constraints whose gradients at the starting\npoint are linearly dependent on those of the others\n( -1 : not computed) logical, public :: probe_not_finite = .false. level 3 : whether f or c is not finite at one of the two\npoints probed next to the starting point character(len=:), public, allocatable :: problem_report the report on the starting point (level >= 2 ), as\nprinted before the iteration log: its lines, each\nended by a newline character character(len=:), public, allocatable :: report the diagnosis of the solve, as printed after the\nsummary: its lines, each ended by a newline character type, public :: sqpopt_iter_info information about one major iteration, for the iteration log Components Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial real(kind=wp), public :: f = 0.0_wp objective at the start of the iteration (of the scaled problem) real(kind=wp), public :: kkt = 0.0_wp KKT error there (se