 Derived Types type, public :: sqpopt_trust_region_type options and state for trust-region-based globalization\n(an alternative to linesearch%search , see module docs). Components Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial logical, public :: enabled = .false. if true, use trust-region radius management instead of a line search real(kind=wp), public :: radius0 = 1.0_wp initial trust-region radius real(kind=wp), public :: radius_min = 1.0e-8_wp below this, a major iteration's retries give up (no step is taken) real(kind=wp), public :: radius_max = 1.0e3_wp ceiling on the radius real(kind=wp), public :: eta1 = 0.1_wp ratio threshold to accept a step (merit-ratio acceptance only) real(kind=wp), public :: eta2 = 0.75_wp ratio threshold to also grow the radius (merit-ratio acceptance only) real(kind=wp), public :: shrink_factor = 0.5_wp radius *= shrink_factor on a rejected step real(kind=wp), public :: expand_factor = 2.0_wp radius *= expand_factor on a step that used the full radius and was accepted integer, public :: max_retries = 20 maximum QP re-solves (with a shrinking radius) per major iteration logical, public :: ready = .false. whether radius has been initialized from radius0 yet real(kind=wp), public :: radius = 0.0_wp current trust-region radius type( sqpopt_log_type ), public :: log logical, public :: used_soc = .false. Type-Bound Procedures procedure, public :: step => trust_region_step Subroutines private  subroutine trust_region_step (me, problem, hessian, qp_solver, linesearch, x, g, f, c, jac, x_new, new_lambda, alpha, istat, kkt, inertia, least_squares) attempt to find and accept a trust-region step, re-solving the QP\n subproblem with a shrinking radius as needed (see the module-level\n documentation for the full algorithm). Updates me%radius in place. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( sqpopt_trust_region_type ), intent(inout) :: me type( sqpopt_problem_type ), intent(inout) :: problem problem definition type( sqpopt_hessian_type ), intent(inout) :: hessian matrix-free Hessian approximation type( sqpopt_qp_solver_type ), intent(inout) :: qp_solver QP subproblem solver type( sqpopt_linesearch_type ), intent(inout) :: linesearch supplies the merit function ( merit , ratio test) or\nthe filter ( filter , mode==sqpopt_linesearch_filter )\nor funnel ( funnel , mode==sqpopt_linesearch_funnel ) real(kind=wp), intent(in), dimension(:) :: x current point dimension(n) real(kind=wp), intent(in), dimension(:) :: g objective gradient at x dimension(n) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: f objective value at x real(kind=wp), intent(in), dimension(:) :: c constraint values at x dimension(m) type( sqpopt_sparse_matrix ), intent(in) :: jac constraint Jacobian at x , dimension(m,n) real(kind=wp), intent(out), dimension(:) :: x_new new point dimension(n) ( x if no retry was accepted) real(kind=wp), intent(out), dimension(:) :: new_lambda new multipliers dimension(m) , from the QP solve that produced x_new real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: alpha 1 if a step was accepted, 0 otherwise (informational only -- there\nis no line-search step length under trust-region globalization) integer, intent(out) :: istat status code (see sqpopt_types_module ) type( sqpopt_kkt_type ), intent(inout), optional :: kkt the KKT matrix, for the QP solver's direct method\n(see solve_qp_subproblem ) type( sqpopt_inertia_type ), intent(inout), optional :: inertia the inertia control, for the same type( sqpopt_least_squares_type ), intent(inout), optional :: least_squares the direct least-squares solver, for\nthe second-order correction (see soc_step )","tags":"","url":"module/sqpopt_trust_region_module.html"},{"title":"sqpopt_inertia_module – sqpopt","text":"Inertia control for the Hessians that can be indefinite, the exact one\nand SR1 ( options%inertia_control ): the shift of is found from a sparse factorization of the KKT\nmatrix of the QP subproblem's working set (see sqpopt_kkt_module ),\nby the sparse solver of options%linear_solver (MUMPS or QDLDL; with\nthe exact Hessian, MUMPS is the better one, see sqpopt_symmetric_solver_module ). The QP subproblem's step is only a minimizer if the Hessian is positive\ndefinite on the null space of the working set's constraints, . The factorization of the KKT matrix tells how many\ndirections of negative curvature that null space has, so the smallest\nshift that leaves none is found by refactoring ( inertia_correct ),\nmuch as in IPOPT: first the current shift, then shift_min times the\nsize of the Hessian (or a third of the last shift that was needed, if\nthat is larger), then 8 times as much at each attempt, up to shift_max . (IPOPT multiplies by 100 until a shift has been needed\nonce. On the Hock-Schittkowski problems that was no better: 273 solved\nand 3 failed, against 274 and 2, with 1% more function evaluations.\nFactors of 2, 4, and 16 gave 271 or 272 solved.) This only decides the shift. The QP subproblems are solved by sqpopt_qp_solver_module with the shifted Hessian (see sqpopt_iterate ), which can reuse the factorization for a direct step\n(see sqpopt_qp_direct_module ). Uses sqpopt_types_module sqpopt_hessian_module sqpopt_kinds sqpopt_kkt_module module~~sqpopt_inertia_module~~UsesGraph module~sqpopt_inertia_module sqpopt_inertia_module module~sqpopt_hessian_module sqpopt_hessian_module module~sqpopt_inertia_module->module~sqpopt_hessian_module module~sqpopt_kinds sqpopt_kinds module~sqpopt_inertia_module->module~sqpopt_kinds module~sqpopt_kkt_module sqpopt_kkt_module module~sqpopt_inertia_module->module~sqpopt_kkt_module module~sqpopt_types_module sqpopt_types_module module~sqpopt_inertia_module->module~sqpopt_types_module module~sqpopt_hessian_module->module~sqpopt_kinds module~sqpopt_dense_linalg_module sqpopt_dense_linalg_module module~sqpopt_hessian_module->module~sqpopt_dense_linalg_module iso_fortran_env iso_fortran_env module~sqpopt_kinds->iso_fortran_env module~sqpopt_kkt_module->module~sqpopt_hessian_module module~sqpopt_kkt_module->mod