ertia_known = .true. of the last factorization: whether n_negative and n_null are\nthe matrix's (else they are those of the factors, which are not\nthe matrix's: see the backend's documentation) logical, public :: out_of_memory = .false. whether an allocation of the backend failed (it stays set) integer, private :: n = 0 order of the matrix integer, private, dimension(:), allocatable :: irow row indices of the pattern's entries integer, private, dimension(:), allocatable :: icol column indices of the pattern's entries real(kind=wp), private, dimension(:,:), allocatable :: a the matrix last factored dimension(n,n) real(kind=wp), private, dimension(:,:), allocatable :: lu its LU factors dimension(n,n) integer, private, dimension(:), allocatable :: piv the row pivots of the LU factorization dimension(n) Type-Bound Procedures procedure, public :: start => dense_start procedure, public :: refactor => dense_refactor procedure, public :: back_solve => dense_back_solve procedure, public :: multiply => dense_multiply procedure, public :: free => dense_free Subroutines private  subroutine dense_start (me, n, irow, icol, ok, threads, signs) keep the pattern, and allocate the dense matrices. ok is false if the\norder exceeds dense_max_order , or the matrices can't be allocated. threads and signs are not used (this backend pivots, and is\nsingle-threaded). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( sqpopt_dense_ldl_type ), intent(inout) :: me integer, intent(in) :: n order of the matrix integer, intent(in), dimension(:) :: irow row indices of the entries dimension(nnz) integer, intent(in), dimension(:) :: icol column indices of the entries dimension(nnz) logical, intent(out) :: ok whether the backend is ready integer, intent(in), optional :: threads (not used) integer, intent(in), optional, dimension(:) :: signs (not used) private  subroutine dense_refactor (me, val, ok) form the dense matrix from the values val , count its inertia, and\nfactor it (see the module documentation). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( sqpopt_dense_ldl_type ), intent(inout) :: me real(kind=wp), intent(in), dimension(:) :: val values of the entries dimension(nnz) logical, intent(out) :: ok whether the factorization succeeded private pure subroutine lu_factor_null_safe (a, piv) in-place LU factorization with partial pivoting of the dense matrix a , in which a negligible pivot (a null column, below the diagonal) is\nreplaced by a large one, so that the factorization never fails (see the\nmodule documentation). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(inout), dimension(:,:) :: a matrix, overwritten by its L (unit, below the diagonal)\nand U factors integer, intent(out), dimension(:) :: piv piv(p) is the row swapped with row p at step p private  subroutine dense_back_solve (me, v, ok) one solve with the LU factors, without refinement. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( sqpopt_dense_ldl_type ), intent(inout) :: me real(kind=wp), intent(inout), dimension(:) :: v the right-hand side, overwritten by the solution logical, intent(out) :: ok whether it was solved private  subroutine dense_multiply (me, x, y) the product with the values last factored. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( sqpopt_dense_ldl_type ), intent(in) :: me real(kind=wp), intent(in), dimension(:) :: x the vector dimension(n) real(kind=wp), intent(out), dimension(:) :: y the product dimension(n) private  subroutine dense_free (me) free everything. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( sqpopt_dense_ldl_type ), intent(inout) :: me","tags":"","url":"module/sqpopt_dense_ldl_module.html"},{"title":"sqpopt_filter_module – sqpopt","text":"The filter (Fletcher & Leyffer, \"Nonlinear programming without a\npenalty function\" , Math. Program. 91 (2002)), with the globally\nconvergent rules of Wächter & Biegler ( \"Line search filter methods for\nnonlinear programming: motivation and global convergence\" , SIAM J.\nOptim. 16 (2005), and the IPOPT paper, Math. Program. 106 (2006)): the\nacceptance test of the filter line search (see sqpopt_linesearch_module 's filter_line_search ) and of the trust\nregion with the filter (see sqpopt_trust_region_module ), and the\nfilter itself, which persists across major iterations. A trial point is judged by the pair of constraint violation and objective value, and must not be\ndominated by the filter. A switching condition decides whether a step\nmust reduce the objective (an Armijo test, \"f-type\" step) or may trade\nobjective for feasibility; only non-f-type steps enlarge the filter\n(see filter_step_acceptable ). Uses sqpopt_types_module sqpopt_kinds module~~sqpopt_filter_module~~UsesGraph module~sqpopt_filter_module sqpopt_filter_module module~sqpopt_kinds sqpopt_kinds module~sqpopt_filter_module->module~sqpopt_kinds module~sqpopt_types_module sqpopt_types_module module~sqpopt_filter_module->module~sqpopt_types_module iso_fortran_env iso_fortran_env module~sqpopt_kinds->iso_fortran_env module~sqpopt_types_module->module~sqpopt_kinds ieee_arithmetic ieee_arithmetic module~sqpopt_types_module->ieee_arithmetic Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Used by module~~sqpopt_filter_module~~UsedByGraph module~sqpopt_filter_module sqpopt_filter_module module~sqpopt_linesearch_module sqpopt_linesearch_module module~sqpopt_linesearch_module->module~sqpopt_filter_module module~sqpopt_iterate_module sqpopt_iterate_module module~sqpopt_iterate_module->module~sqpopt_linesearch_module module~sqpopt_options_module sqpopt_options_module module~sqpopt_iterate_module->module~sqpopt_options_module module~sqpopt_restoration_module sqpopt_restoration_module module~sqpopt_iterate_module->module~sqpopt_restoration_module module~sqpopt_trust_region_module sqpopt_trust_region_module module~sqpopt_iterate_module->module~sqpopt_trust_region_module module~sqpopt_diagnostics_module sqpopt_diagnostics_module module~sqpopt_iterate_module->module~sqpopt_diagnostics_module module~sqpopt_module sqpopt_module module~sqpopt_module->module~sqpopt_linesearch_module module~sqpopt_module->module~sqpopt_iterate_module module~sqpopt_module->module~sqpopt_options_module module~sqpopt_module->module~sqpopt_restoration_module module~sqpopt_module->module~sqpopt_trust_region_module module~sqpopt_module->module~sqpopt_diagnostics_module module~sqpopt_nlls_module sqpopt_nlls_module module~sqpopt_nlls_module->module~sqpopt_linesearch_module module~sqpopt_nlls_module->module~sqpopt_module module~sqpopt_nlls_module->module~sqpopt_options_module module~sqpopt_nlls_module->module~sqpopt_trust_region_module module~sqpopt_options_module->module~sqpopt_linesearch_module module~sqpopt_options_module->module~sqpopt_restoration_module module~sqpopt_restoration_module->module~sqpopt_linesearch_module module~sqpopt_trust_region_module->module~sqpopt_linesearch_module module~sqpopt_diagnostics_module->module~sqpopt_options_module Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Derived Types type, public :: sqpopt_filter_type options and state of the filter (the filter component of sqpopt_linesearch_type ), with the default values from\nWächter & Biegler. Components Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial real(kind=wp), public :: gamma_theta = 1.0e-5_wp margin : a step must reduce by this fraction... real(kind=wp), public :: gamma_phi = 1.0e-5_wp ...or reduce by real(kind=wp), public :: delta = 1.0_wp switching condition constant real(kind=wp), public :: s_theta = 1.1_wp switching condition exponent real(kind=wp), public :: s_phi = 2.3_wp switching condition exponent real(kind=wp), public :: eta_phi = 1.0e-4_wp Armijo constant for f-type steps real(kind=wp), public :: theta_max_fact = 1.0e4_wp this : no point with a larger violation is accepted real(kind=wp), public :: theta_min_fact = 1.0e-4_wp this : below it, f-type steps are allowed real(kind=wp), public :: gamma_alpha = 0.05_wp safety factor in the minimum step length before restoration logical, public :: ready = .false. whether the filter below has been initialized real(kind=wp), public :: theta_max = 0.0_wp real(kind=wp), public :: theta_min = 0.0_wp real(kind=wp), public, dimension(:), allocatable :: theta constraint-violation value of each filter entry real(kind=wp), public, dimension(:), allocatable :: phi objective value of each filter entry Type-Bound Procedures procedure, public :: prepare => filter_prepare_state procedure, public :: accept => filter_step_acceptable procedure, public :: record => filter_augment procedure, public :: min_step => filter_min_step procedure, public :: acceptable => filter_point_acceptable Functions private  function filter_step_acceptable (me, theta_k, phi_k, gtp, alpha, theta_t, phi_t, f_type) result(ok) whether a trial point with violation theta_t and objective phi_t ,\nreached with step length alpha from the current point\n( theta_k , phi_k ), is acceptable (see filter_line_search for the\nrules). gtp is the predicted change in the objective along the full\nstep ( for the line search; the trust region passes the\nquadratic model's , with alpha=1 ). f_type is set if the\nswitching condition held (so the step was judged on the objective alone,\nand must not enlarge the filter). The trial point must also be\nacceptable to the filter itself: , and not\ndominated by any filter entry ( or for every entry j ). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( sqpopt_filter_type ), intent(in) :: me real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: theta_k violation and objective at the current point real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: phi_k violation and objective at the current point real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: gtp predicted change in the objective along the full step real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: alpha step length real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: theta_t violation and objective at the trial point real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: phi_t violation and objective at the trial point logical, intent(out) :: f_type true if the switching condition held Return Value logical private pure function filter_min_step (me, theta_k, gtp) result(alpha_min) Wächter & Biegler's minimum step length : below it,\nno trial step can be acceptable (so the line search should give up and\ngo to feasibility restoration). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( sqpopt_filter_type ), intent(in) :: me real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: theta_k violation at the current point real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: gtp Return Value real(kind=wp) private  function filter_point_acceptable (me, theta, phi) result(ok) whether a point with violation theta and objective phi is acceptable\nto the filter: , and not dominated by any\nfilter entry (always true before the filter is initialized). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( sqpopt_filter_type ), intent(in) :: me real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: theta constraint violation real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: phi objective Return Value logical Subroutines private  subroutine filter_prepare_state (me, theta0) initialize the filter (empty) and its bounds , from the constraint violation theta0 at the\nstarting point, the first time it is used; a no-op after that. Shared\nby filter_line_search and the trust region's filter acceptance, so\nboth use the same filter. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( sqpopt_filter_type ), intent(inout) :: me real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: theta0 constraint violation at the starting point private  subroutine filter_augment (me, theta_k, phi_k) augment the filter with the current point ( theta_k , phi_k ), with\nmargins: the entry is added, and any existing entries\nit dominates are removed. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( sqpopt_filter_type ), intent(inout) :: me real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: theta_k violation and objective at the current point real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: phi_k violation and objective at the current point","tags":"","url":"module/sqpopt_filter_module.html"},{"title":"sqpopt_diagnostics_module – sqpopt","text":"Diagnostics of a solve, to help when it doesn't converge (see options%diagnostic_level ). The iteration log says what happened at\neach iteration; the diagnostics say which constraints and variables are\nresponsible, and what the final status most likely means. They are\nopt-in, by level: 1 : a diagnosis of the final point ( diagnostics_finish ): the\n  constraints with the largest violations and multipliers, the variables\n  with the largest stationarity residuals, the active set and its\n  degeneracy (multipliers that are zero or have the wrong sign, active\n  gradients that are linearly dependent), the last QP subproblem (its\n  elastic constraints), and a verdict for the final status. It uses the\n  values the solver has at the final point anyway. 2 : also a report on the starting point ( diagnostics_start : the\n  sizes of the gradients, which show how the problem is scaled, and the\n  structure of the constraints), and what the iterations showed: the\n  rate of convergence, the step lengths, a working set that flips between\n  two states, the iteration that took the most time\n  ( diagnostics_record ), and constraints whose changes along the steps\n  disagree with their derivatives ( diagnostics_point ). With options%diagnostics_unit , the history of the iterations is also\n  written to a file, as comma-separated values. 3 : also the diagnostics that evaluate the user's functions: f and c at two points next to the starting point, to see whether it is at\n  the edge of their domain. Levels 0 to 2 call the user's functions exactly as often as a solve\nwithout diagnostics: everything is computed from values the solver has\nevaluated (through the problem's evaluation caches), and no level\nchanges the iterates. The results are returned in results%diagnosis (see sqpopt_diagnosis_type ), whose report and problem_report are the texts the solver prints (if options%print_level >= 1 ). The derivative check of level 2 needs no evaluations. Between two\nconsecutive iterates and , the change of a\nfunction is up to a term\nof the third order in (the trapezoid rule, exact for a quadratic),\nand the solver has the values and the derivatives at both. A constraint\n(or the objective) whose actual changes differ from this by more than\n20% in most of the steps has derivatives that don't match its values.\nOnly steps that change no variable by more than 10% of its size are\nused, so that the third-order term is small. Uses sqpopt_problem_module sqpopt_linalg_module sqpopt_qp_solver_module sqpopt_types_module ieee_arithmetic sqpopt_options_module sqpopt_log_module iso_fortran_env sqpopt_kinds module~~sqpopt_diagnostics_module~~UsesGraph module~sqpopt_diagnostics_module sqpopt_diagnostics_module ieee_arithmetic ieee_arithmetic module~sqpopt_diagnostics_module->ieee_arithmetic iso_fortran_env iso_fortran_env module~sqpopt_diagnostics_module->iso_fortran_env module~sqpopt_kinds sqpopt_kinds module~sqpopt_diagnostics_module->module~sqpopt_kinds module~sqpopt_linalg_module sqpopt_linalg_module module~sqpopt_diagnostics_module->module~sqpopt_linalg_module module~sqpopt_log_module sqpopt_log_module module~sqpopt_diagnostics_module->module~sqpopt_log_module module~sqpopt_options_module sqpopt_options_module module~sqpopt_diagnostics_module->module~sqpopt_options_module module~sqpopt_problem_module sqpopt_problem_module modul