bda, x_prev, gl_prev, f_prev, viol_prev, jac, n_acceptable, n_stalled, n_escape, restoration, inertia, kkt, least_squares, diagnostics, iter, report, done, istat, info) perform one major SQP iteration, updating x and lambda in place. x_prev / gl_prev / f_prev hold the previous point, the Lagrangian\n gradient there (evaluated with the multipliers passed back out in lambda , as the quasi-Newton update requires), and the objective value.\n They are used to form the quasi-Newton (s,y) pair and for the\n stalled-progress and infeasibility tests. Pass them in unallocated before the first call. The Hessian update and those two tests are\n skipped on the first iteration, since there is no previous point yet. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( sqpopt_problem_type ), intent(inout) :: problem problem definition type( sqpopt_options_type ), intent(in) :: options solver options type( sqpopt_hessian_type ), intent(inout) :: hessian Hessian of the Lagrangian approximation type( sqpopt_qp_solver_type ), intent(inout) :: qp_solver QP subproblem solver type( sqpopt_linesearch_type ), intent(inout) :: linesearch merit function / line search type( sqpopt_trust_region_type ), intent(inout) :: trust_region trust-region globalization (used instead of linesearch when trust_region%enabled ) real(kind=wp), intent(inout), dimension(:) :: x current point, updated on exit dimension(n) real(kind=wp), intent(inout), dimension(:) :: lambda current Lagrange multipliers, updated on exit dimension(m) real(kind=wp), intent(inout), dimension(:), allocatable :: x_prev previous point (unallocated before the 1st call) real(kind=wp), intent(inout), dimension(:), allocatable :: gl_prev previous Lagrangian gradient (unallocated before the 1st call) real(kind=wp), intent(inout), allocatable :: f_prev previous objective value (unallocated before the 1st call) real(kind=wp), intent(inout), allocatable :: viol_prev previous constraint violation (unallocated before the 1st call) type( sqpopt_sparse_matrix ), intent(inout) :: jac workspace for the constraint Jacobian: its sparsity\nstructure is set on the first call (when jac%val is\nunallocated) and reused, and its values are updated integer, intent(inout) :: n_acceptable number of consecutive iterations (so far) at which the\nacceptable-level test has held ( 0 before the 1st call) integer, intent(inout) :: n_stalled number of consecutive iterations (so far) at which the\nstalled-progress test has held ( 0 before the 1st call) integer, intent(inout) :: n_escape number of second-order escapes from a stationary point of\nthe violation taken so far ( 0 before the 1st call) type( sqpopt_restoration_type ), intent(inout) :: restoration feasibility restoration phase state (see sqpopt_restoration_module ) type( sqpopt_inertia_type ), intent(inout) :: inertia inertia control of the exact or SR1 Hessian (used if inertia%enabled , see sqpopt_inertia_module ) type( sqpopt_kkt_type ), intent(inout) :: kkt the KKT matrix of the QP's working set, for the inertia\ncontrol and the QP solver's direct method (used if kkt%enabled , see sqpopt_kkt_module ) type( sqpopt_least_squares_type ), intent(inout) :: least_squares direct least-squares solver, for the\nrestoration steps and second-order corrections (used\nif least_squares%enabled , see sqpopt_least_squares_module ) type( sqpopt_diagnostics_type ), intent(inout) :: diagnostics the diagnostics of the solve, which note each\niterate (see options%diagnostic_level and sqpopt_diagnostics_module ) integer, intent(in) :: iter major iteration number (starts at 1), passed to report procedure( sqpopt_report_func ), optional, pointer :: report optional user progress-reporting callback (see sqpopt_types_module ) logical, intent(out) :: done true if the solver should stop at x (see istat for why) integer, intent(out) :: istat status code (see above and sqpopt_types_module ) type( sqpopt_iter_info ), intent(out) :: info information about this iteration, for the log public  subroutine sqpopt_evaluate_point (problem, options, x, lambda, jac, f, c, kkt, feas, z, stat_error) evaluate the (scaled) problem at x , and the resulting KKT and\nfeasibility errors and variable-bound multipliers z (with the\nconstraint multipliers lambda ): for a variable\nat one of its bounds, zero otherwise (for the Lagrangian ). Used to report the final state of a solve. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( sqpopt_problem_type ), intent(inout) :: problem problem definition type( sqpopt_options_type ), intent(in) :: options solver options real(kind=wp), intent(in), dimension(:) :: x point dimension(n) real(kind=wp), intent(in), dimension(:) :: lambda constraint multipliers dimension(m) type( sqpopt_sparse_matrix ), intent(inout) :: jac Jacobian workspace (as for sqpopt_iterate ) real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: f objective at x real(kind=wp), intent(out), dimension(:) :: c constraints at x dimension(m) real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: kkt KKT error at x real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: feas feasibility error at x real(kind=wp), intent(out), dimension(:) :: z variable-bound multipliers dimension(n) real(kind=wp), intent(out), optional :: stat_error the stationarity residual (of the scaled problem,\nwithout the multiplier scaling; see check_convergence )","tags":"","url":"module/sqpopt_iterate_module.html"},{"title":"sqpopt_funnel_module – sqpopt","text":"The funnel (Kiessling, Leyffer & Vanaret, \"A unified funnel\nrestoration SQP algorithm\" , Math. Program. (2025); as implemented in\nthe Uno solver): the acceptance test of the funnel line search (see sqpopt_linesearch_module 's funnel_line_search ) and of the trust\nregion with the funnel (see sqpopt_trust_region_module ), and the\nfunnel width, which persists across major iterations. Like the filter (see sqpopt_filter_module ), there is no merit\nfunction or penalty parameter, but the filter's list of points is\nreplaced by a single number, the funnel width , a bound on the constraint violation that shrinks as the iterations\nprogress. A trial point must be inside the funnel; a switching\ncondition then decides whether it must reduce the objective (an Armijo\ntest, \"f-type\") or sufficiently reduce the violation relative to the\nfunnel (\"h-type\", which shrinks the funnel). See funnel_step_acceptable . Uses sqpopt_types_module sqpopt_kinds module~~sqpopt_funnel_module~~UsesGraph module~sqpopt_funnel_module sqpopt_funnel_module module~sqpopt_kinds sqpopt_kinds module~sqpopt_funnel_module->module~sqpopt_kinds module~sqpopt_types_module sqpopt_types_module module~sqpopt_funnel_module->module~sqpopt_types_module iso_fortran_env iso_fortran_env module~sqpopt_kinds->iso_fortran_env module~sqpopt_types_module->module~sqpopt_kinds ieee_arithmetic ieee_arithmetic module~sqpopt_types_module->ieee_arithmetic Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Used by module~~sqpopt_funnel_module~~UsedByGraph module~sqpopt_funnel_module sqpopt_funnel_module module~sqpopt_linesearch_module sqpopt_linesearch_module module~sqpopt_linesearch_module->module~sqpopt_funnel_module module~sqpopt_iterate_module sqpopt_iterate_module module~sqpopt_iterate_module->module~sqpopt_linesearch_module module~sqpopt_options_module sqpopt_options_module module~sqpopt_iterate_module->module~sqpopt_options_module module~sqpopt_restoration_module sqpopt_restoration_module module~sqpopt_iterate_module->module~sqpopt_restoration_module module~sqpopt_trust_region_module sqpopt_trust_region_module module~sqpopt_iterate_module->module~sqpopt_trust_region_module module~sqpopt_diagnostics_module sqpopt_diagnostics_module module~sqpopt_iterate_module->module~sqpopt_diagnostics_module module~sqpopt_module sqpopt_module module~sqpopt_module->module~sqpopt_linesearch_module module~sqpopt_module->module~sqpopt_iterate_module module~sqpopt_module->module~sqpopt_options_module module~sqpopt_module->module~sqpopt_restoration_module module~sqpopt_module->module~sqpopt_trust_region_module module~sqpopt_module->module~sqpopt_diagnostics_module module~sqpopt_nlls_module sqpopt_nlls_module module~sqpopt_nlls_module->module~sqpopt_linesearch_module module~sqpopt_nlls_module->module~sqpopt_module module~sqpopt_nlls_module->module~sqpopt_options_module module~sqpopt_nlls_module->module~sqpopt_trust_region_module module~sqpopt_options_module->module~sqpopt_linesearch_module module~sqpopt_options_module->module~sqpopt_restoration_module module~sqpopt_restoration_module->module~sqpopt_linesearch_module module~sqpopt_trust_region_module->module~sqpopt_linesearch_module module~sqpopt_diagnostics_module->module~sqpopt_options_module Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Derived Types type, public :: sqpopt_funnel_type options and state of the funnel (the funnel component of sqpopt_linesearch_type ), with the default values of the Uno\nsolver. Components Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial real(kind=wp), public :: width_min = 1.0_wp initial funnel width this, width_fact real(kind=wp), public :: width_fact = 1.5_wp see width_min real(kind=wp), public :: beta = 0.9999_wp an h-type step must reach ( ) real(kind=wp), public :: kappa = 0.5_wp after an h-type step, the new width is (at least) the convex\ncombination (see update ) integer, public :: update = 1 funnel width update after an h-type step: 1 = if the\nviolation decreased, else ; 2 = real(kind=wp), public :: delta = 0.999_wp switching condition constant : an f-type step needs real(kind=wp), public :: s_theta = 2.0_wp switching condition exponent real(kind=wp), public :: eta = 1.0e-4_wp Armijo constant for f-type steps logical, public :: require_current = .false. also require every trial point to be acceptable with respect to\nthe current point: or real(kind=wp), public :: gamma = 1.0e-3_wp in require_current logical, public :: ready = .false. whether the funnel width below has been initialized real(kind=wp), public :: width = 0.0_wp the funnel width Type-Bound Procedures procedure, public :: prepare => funnel_prepare_state procedure, public :: accept => funnel_step_acceptable procedure, public :: record => funnel_shrink procedure, public :: restoration => funnel_shrink_restoration procedure, public :: acceptable => funnel_point_acceptable Functions private  function funnel_step_acceptable (me, theta_k, phi_k, pred, theta_t, phi_t, f_type) result(ok) whether a trial point with violation theta_t and objective phi_t is\nacceptable to the funnel, from the current point ( theta_k , phi_k )\n(see funnel_line_search for the rules). pred is the predicted\ndecrease in the objective ( for the line search; the\ntrust region passes the quadratic model's decrease q ). f_type is set\nif the switching condition held (so the step was judged on the objective\nalone, and must not shrink the funnel). Doesn't change the funnel: the\ncaller shrinks it after accepting an h-type step (see funnel_shrink ). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( sqpopt_funnel_type ), intent(in) :: me real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: theta_k violation and objective at the current point real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: phi_k violation and objective at the current point real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: pred predicted decrease in the objective real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: theta_t violation and objective at the trial point real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: phi_t violation and objective at the trial point logical, intent(out) :: f_type true if the switching condition held Return Value logical private  function funnel_point_acceptable (me, theta) result(ok) whether a point with violation theta is inside the funnel, (always true before the funnel is initialized). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( sqpopt_funnel_type ), intent(in) :: me real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: theta constraint violation Return Value logical Subroutines private  subroutine funnel_prepare_state (me, theta_k) initialize the funnel width from the constraint violation theta0 at\nthe starting point, the first time it is used: width_min , width_fact . After that, it only makes sure the current\npoint is inside the funnel, (a restoration or\nescape step reduces a different measure of the violation, so it can\noccasionally end slightly outside). Shared by funnel_line_search and\nthe trust region's funnel acceptance. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( sqpopt_funnel_type ), intent(inout) :: me real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: theta_k constraint violation at the current point private  subroutine funnel_shrink (me, theta_k, theta_t) shrink the funnel after an accepted h-type step from violation theta_k to theta_t (see update for the two rules). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( sqpopt_funnel_type ), intent(inout) :: me real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: theta_k violation at the current point real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: theta_t violation at the accepted point private  subroutine funnel_shrink_restoration (me, theta_k) shrink the funnel toward the current violation theta_k before a\nfeasibility restoration step, so the iterations can't cycle back to the\ncurrent point: . Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( sqpopt_funnel_type ), intent(inout) :: me real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: theta_k violation at the current point","tags":"","url":"module/sqpopt_funnel_module.html"},{"title":"sqpopt_qp_solver_module – sqpopt","text":"Solves the quadratic programming (QP) subproblem generated at each\nmajor SQP iteration: subject to the linearized constraints and variable bounds: The subproblem is solved by one of two active-set QP solvers, selected\nby mode : sqpopt_qp_dense : a dense active-set QP (see sqpopt_qp_dense_module ); sqpopt_qp_reduced_hessian : a sparse/matrix-free active-set QP (see sqpopt_qp_reduced_hessian_module ); sqpopt_qp_auto (the default): sqpopt_qp_dense when n <= auto_dense_max_n , else sqpopt_qp_reduced_hessian . Before either is run, the unconstrained step is tried (unless unconstrained_step is false): with the limited-memory BFGS Hessian,\nwhich is positive definite, the minimizer of the QP's objective alone is , which the two-loop recursion gives in O(nk) operations for k stored pairs (see hessian_inverse_vector_product ).\nIf that step satisfies the bounds and the linearized constraints, it is\nthe solution of the QP, with zero multipliers, and no QP solver is run.\nThat is every QP of a problem without constraints whose bounds aren't\nactive, where the active-set solvers would otherwise work with every\nvariable free (the sparse one by conjugate gradients on a reduced\nHessian of order n ). When the step isn't feasible, the attempt costs\none such product. With direct ( options%direct_qp ), the\nsubproblem is then tried directly, by factoring the KKT matrix of the\nworking set that the active-set solver would start from (see sqpopt_qp_direct_module ); the active-set solver is only run if that\ndoesn't give the solution within direct_max_changes changes of the\nworking set. Both enforce the variable bounds and the linearized constraints exactly\nas part of the QP solve. The step length is then capped at max_step*step_scale (a trust-region-style safeguard), where the major\niterations adapt step_scale like a trust radius: it doubles after a\ncapped step that the line search accepted in full, and halves (down to\n1) after a shortened one. Each solve starts with step_scale = max(1, ||x0||_inf/max_step) , so the cap starts at max_step : relative to the\nsize of the variables, and a solution far away is still reached in a\nfew iterations. Uses sqpopt_qp_reduced_hessian_module sqpopt_qp_dense_module sqpopt_hessian_module sqpopt_linalg_module sqpopt_types_module sqpopt_kkt_module sqpopt_qp_direct_module sqpopt_inertia_module iso_fortran_env sqpopt_kinds module~~sqpopt_qp_solver_module~~UsesGraph module~sqpopt_qp_solver_module sqpopt_qp_solver_module iso_fortran_env iso_fortran_env module~sqpopt_qp_solver_module->iso_fortran_env module~sqpopt_hessian_module sqpopt_hessian_module module~sqpopt_qp_solver_module->module~sqpopt_hessian_module module~sqpopt_inertia_module sqpopt_inertia_module module~sqpopt_qp_solver_module->module~sqpopt_inertia_module module~sqpopt_kinds sqpopt_kinds module~sqpopt_qp_solver_module->module~sqpopt_kinds module~sqpopt_kkt_module sqpopt_kkt_module module~sqpopt_qp_solver_module->module~sqpopt_kkt_module module~sqpopt_linalg_module sqpopt_linalg_module module~sqpopt_qp_solver_module->module~sqpopt_linalg_module module~sqpopt_qp_dense_module sqpopt_qp_dense_module module~sqpopt_qp_solver_module->module~sqpopt_qp_dense_module module~sqpopt_qp_direct_module sqpopt_qp_direct_module module~sqpopt_qp_solver_module->module~sqpopt_qp_direct_module module~sqpopt_qp_reduced_hessian_module sqpopt_qp_reduced_hessian_module module~sqpopt_qp_solver_module->module~sqpopt_qp_reduced_hessian_module module~sqpopt_types_module sqpopt_types_module module~sqpopt_qp_solver_module->module~sqpopt_types_module module~sqpopt_hessian_module->module~sqpopt_kinds module~sqpopt_dense_linalg_module sqpopt_dense_linalg_module module~sqpopt_hessian_module->module~sqpopt_dense_linalg_module module~sqpopt_inertia_module->module~sqpopt_hessian_module module~sqpopt_inertia_module->module~sqpopt_kinds module~sqpopt_inertia_module->module~sqpopt_kkt_module module~sqpopt_inertia_module->module~sqpopt_types_module module~sqpopt_kinds->iso_fortran_env module~sqpopt_kkt_module->modu