entation),\nstarting from the working set status . If it succeeds\n( outcome = sqpopt_direct_solved ), p and lambda are the QP's\nsolution and status its working set. Otherwise they are not to be\nused, status is unchanged, and outcome says why it gave up (see the sqpopt_direct_* constants). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( sqpopt_kkt_type ), intent(inout) :: kkt the KKT matrix (see sqpopt_kkt_module ) type( sqpopt_hessian_type ), intent(inout) :: hessian the Hessian (exact, with its shift, or quasi-Newton) type( sqpopt_sparse_matrix ), intent(in) :: jac sparse constraint Jacobian, dimension(m,n) real(kind=wp), intent(in), dimension(:) :: x current point dimension(n) real(kind=wp), intent(in), dimension(:) :: g objective gradient dimension(n) real(kind=wp), intent(in), dimension(:) :: c current constraint values dimension(m) real(kind=wp), intent(in), dimension(:) :: x_lb variable lower bounds dimension(n) real(kind=wp), intent(in), dimension(:) :: x_ub variable upper bounds dimension(n) real(kind=wp), intent(in), dimension(:) :: c_lb constraint lower bounds dimension(m) real(kind=wp), intent(in), dimension(:) :: c_ub constraint upper bounds dimension(m) integer, intent(in) :: max_changes maximum number of changes of the working set real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: tol relative tolerance for a violated row or bound, and for\nthe sign of a multiplier integer, intent(inout), dimension(:) :: status the working set: the side ( -1 lower, +1 upper, 0 not in it) of each general row, then of each variable\nbound dimension(m+n) real(kind=wp), intent(out), dimension(:) :: p the step dimension(n) real(kind=wp), intent(out), dimension(:) :: lambda the constraint multipliers dimension(m) integer, intent(out) :: n_changes number of changes of the working set that were made integer, intent(out) :: outcome how it ended (a sqpopt_direct_* constant) type( sqpopt_inertia_type ), intent(inout), optional :: inertia the inertia control, to raise the Hessian's shift\nat a 