d from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer, public, parameter :: sqpopt_module_wp = real64 Real working precision if not specified [8 bytes]","tags":"","url":"module/sqpopt_kinds.html"},{"title":"sqpopt_log_module – sqpopt","text":"The detailed log ( options%print_level >= 3 ): the components that print\ndetails of their work (the line search and the trust region) each hold a sqpopt_log_type , set from options%print_level and options%output_unit at the start of each solve (so separate solver\nobjects log independently). Also the number formatting shared by the log\nlines. Uses sqpopt_types_module iso_fortran_env sqpopt_kinds module~~sqpopt_log_module~~UsesGraph module~sqpopt_log_module sqpopt_log_module iso_fortran_env iso_fortran_env module~sqpopt_log_module->iso_fortran_env module~sqpopt_kinds sqpopt_kinds module~sqpopt_log_module->module~sqpopt_kinds module~sqpopt_types_module sqpopt_types_module module~sqpopt_log_module->module~sqpopt_types_module module~sqpopt_kinds->iso_fortran_env module~sqpopt_types_module->module~sqpopt_kinds ieee_arithmetic ieee_arithmetic module~sqpopt_types_module->ieee_arithmetic Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Used by module~~sqpopt_log_module~~UsedByGraph module~sqpopt_log_module sqpopt_log_module module~sqpopt_diagnostics_module sqpopt_diagnostics_module module~sqpopt_diagnostics_module->module~sqpopt_log_module module~sqpopt_options_module sqpopt_options_module module~sqpopt_diagnostics_module->module~sqpopt_options_module module~sqpopt_iterate_module sqpopt_iterate_module module~sqpopt_iterate_module->module~sqpopt_log_module module~sqpopt_iterate_module->module~sqpopt_diagnostics_module module~sqpopt_linesearch_module sqpopt_linesearch_module module~sqpopt_iterate_module->module~sqpopt_linesearch_module module~sqpopt_trust_region_module sqpopt_trust_region_module module~sqpopt_iterate_module->module~sqpopt_trust_region_module module~sqpopt_iterate_module->module~sqpopt_options_module module~sqpopt_restoration_module sqpopt_restoration_module module~sqpopt_iterate_module->module~sqpopt_restoration_module module~sqpopt_linesearch_module->module~sqpopt_log_module module~sqpopt_module sqpopt_module module~sqpopt_module->module~sqpopt_log_module module~sqpopt_module->module~sqpopt_diagnostics_module module~sqpopt_module->module~sqpopt_iterate_module module~sqpopt_module->module~sqpopt_linesearch_module module~sqpopt_module->module~sqpopt_trust_region_module module~sqpopt_module->module~sqpopt_options_module module~sqpopt_module->module~sqpopt_restoration_module module~sqpopt_trust_region_module->module~sqpopt_log_module module~sqpopt_trust_region_module->module~sqpopt_linesearch_module module~sqpopt_nlls_module sqpopt_nlls_module module~sqpopt_nlls_module->module~sqpopt_linesearch_module module~sqpopt_nlls_module->module~sqpopt_module module~sqpopt_nlls_module->module~sqpopt_trust_region_module module~sqpopt_nlls_module->module~sqpopt_options_module module~sqpopt_options_module->module~sqpopt_linesearch_module module~sqpopt_options_module->module~sqpopt_restoration_module module~sqpopt_restoration_module->module~sqpopt_linesearch_module Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer, public, parameter :: sqpopt_log_detail = 3 the print_level of the detailed log Derived Types type, public :: sqpopt_log_type where, and how much, to print (internal: set by solve ) Components Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer, public :: unit = output_unit Fortran output unit integer, public :: level = 0 options%print_level Type-Bound Procedures procedure, public :: on => log_on procedure, public :: put => log_put Functions private pure function log_on (me, level) whether messages of the given level are printed. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( sqpopt_log_type ), intent(in) :: me integer, intent(in) :: level the print_level a message needs Return Value logical public pure function fmt_e (x) result(s) a real number in the log's ES10.3 style, without padding. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: x the number Return Value character(len=:), allocatable public pure function fmt_g (x) result(s) a real number with more digits ( ES16.9 ), for objective and merit\nvalues, whose changes are often in the later digits. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: x the number Return Value character(len=:), allocatable public pure function fmt_i (i) result(s) an integer, without padding. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: i the number Return Value character(len=:), allocatable public pure function qp_status_text (istat) result(s) a short description of a QP solve's status, for the log. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: istat the QP solve's status code (see sqpopt_types_module ) Return Value character(len=:), allocatable public pure function plural (n, one, many) result(s) a count and a noun, e.g. 1 iteration , 3 iterations . Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: n the count character(len=*), intent(in) :: one the noun, singular character(len=*), intent(in) :: many the noun, plural Return Value character(len=:), allocatable Subroutines private  subroutine log_put (me, level, line) print a detail line (indented under the iteration it belongs to), if\nmessages of the given level are printed. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( sqpopt_log_type ), intent(in) :: me integer, intent(in) :: level the print_level the line needs character(len=*), intent(in) :: line the text (without the indentation, which is added)","tags":"","url":"module/sqpopt_log_module.html"},{"title":"sqpopt_linesearch_module – sqpopt","text":"The line searches used to globalize the SQP iterations (ensures\nprogress towards both optimality and feasibility). The acceptance tests\nthey use are in their own modules, held here as components: the merit\nfunction and its penalty parameter ( merit , see sqpopt_merit_module ), the filter ( filter , see sqpopt_filter_module ), and the funnel ( funnel , see sqpopt_funnel_module ). The trust region (see sqpopt_trust_region_module ) uses the same components, so the two\nglobalizations share the filter or funnel. Five line search strategies are available ( sqpopt_linesearch_type%mode ): sqpopt_linesearch_armijo -- a standard backtracking line search\n  with an Armijo-type sufficient-decrease test on the merit function (as\n  used by default in slsqp ). sqpopt_linesearch_exact -- (approximately) minimizes the merit\n  function along the search direction using the derivative-free fmin routine (from the fmin dependency), rather than a hand-written\n  exact-search implementation. sqpopt_linesearch_watchdog -- Powell's watchdog technique\n  (Chamberlain, Lemarechal, Pedersen & Powell, Math. Prog. Study 16 (1982)): tracks the best point found so\n  far and, for a short window after a genuine improvement, relaxes the\n  sufficient-decrease test to allow the merit function to temporarily\n  get worse (accepting the full quasi-Newton step outright) rather than\n  stalling near a curved/simultaneously-active constraint boundary (the\n  Maratos effect). If the relaxed window is used up without a new best\n  point, it backtracks all the way to the best point found so far and\n  disables relaxed acceptance for watchdog_cooldown_len iterations.\n  This targets the same failure mode as the second-order correction and\n  the augmented Lagrangian merit function, via a different mechanism. sqpopt_linesearch_filter ( default ) -- a filter line search (Fletcher &\n  Leyffer, \"Nonlinear programming without a penalty function\" , Math.\n  Program. 91 (2002)), with the globally convergent line-search rules of\n  Wächter & Biegler ( \"Line search filter methods for nonlinear\n  programming: motivation and global convergence\" , SIAM J. Optim. 16\n  (2005), and the IPOPT paper, Math. Program. 106 (2006)): no merit\n  function or penalty parameter; a trial point is judged by the pair of constraint violation and\n  objective value, and must not be dominated by the filter (see sqpopt_filter_module ). See filter_line_search .\n  It is the default: on the Hock-Schittkowski test set (see test/test_hs_suite.f90 ) it solves the most problems, with the\n  fewest function evaluations, of all the line search / merit function /\n  penalty combinations (and it has no penalty parameter to tune). sqpopt_linesearch_funnel -- the funnel method (Kiessling, Leyffer\n  & Vanaret, \"A unified funnel restoration SQP algorithm\" , Math.\n  Program. (2025); as implemented in the Uno solver): like the filter, no\n  merit function or penalty parameter, but the filter's list of points is\n  replaced by a single number, the funnel width, a bound on the constraint violation that shrinks as the iterations\n  progress. A trial point must be inside the funnel; the same switching\n  condition then decides whether it must reduce the objective (an\n  Armijo test, \"f-type\") or sufficiently reduce the violation relative\n  to the funnel (\"h-type\", which shrinks the funnel). See funnel_line_search . Two options from NLPQLP (Schittkowski) apply to the backtracking\nsearches: interpolate (on by default) chooses each backtracking step\nlength by safeguarded quadratic interpolation (see next_step_length ) rather than a fixed factor; and nonmonotone_len (off by default) retries a failed search non-monotonically, against the\nworst of the recent iterates (not used by the funnel search). On the Hock-Schittkowski test set the\ninterpolation solves one more problem with the filter search, with\nfewer function evaluations (and a third fewer with the merit function); the non-monotone retry doesn't help the filter search,\nbut does help the merit-function ones (e.g. with the augmented\nLagrangian and interpolation, 273 solved instead of 270). All three of the merit-function-based modes start each search from an\ninitial trial step length (see initial_step_length ) rather than always 1 , capped by major_step_limit (SNOPT's \"Major step limit\" option)\nso that no variable can change by more than a factor of major_step_limit relative to its current magnitude in a single major\niteration -- a QP step that is technically feasible can still be\nunreasonably large (e.g. from a poorly-scaled problem or an early,\ninaccurate Hessian approximation), and this guards against the\nresulting merit-function evaluations diverging or becoming undefined. At options%print_level >= 3 , every trial point (step length, merit\nvalue or violation and objective, and whether and why it was accepted)\nis written to the detailed log ( log , see sqpopt_log_module ), and used_soc , used_nonmonotone , and used_relaxed report what the last\nsearch used, for the iteration log's flags. Uses fmin_module sqpopt_types_module sqpopt_merit_module sqpopt_filter_module sqpopt_kinds sqpopt_log_module sqpopt_funnel_module module~~sqpopt_linesearch_module~~UsesGraph module~sqpopt_linesearch_module sqpopt_linesearch_module fmin_module fmin_module module~sqpopt_linesearch_module->fmin_module module~sqpopt_filter_module sqpopt_filter_module module~sqpopt_linesearch_mod